{"raw": {"https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Horticulture_JR0001467": {"title": "Faculty Research Assistant: Horticulture", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nImportant Notifications: Application Deadline: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Current Employees: Do not apply via the OSU Career site. Instead, please login to your regular Workday account and visit the Jobs Hub to apply. Department: Horticulture - Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 31, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Aaron Becerra-Alvarez a.becerraalvarez@oregonstate.edu (707) 380-6563 Job Summary: The Department of Horticulture invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 12-month, fixed-term Faculty Research Assistant position.\u00a0Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. This position will support weed science in vegetable crop production faculty in the Horticulture Department in the College of Agricultural Sciences perform field research. This position collects/provides objective, science-based information related to weed science in vegetable crop production involved in scholarly activities, conducting greenhouse and field research, contributing to publications. The incumbent is expected to maintain and operate field research equipment including but not limited to tractors, planters, mowers, sprayers, lasers, flamers, electric, and other tractor equipment. The incumbent will manage field trials on conventional and organic production. Key Responsibilities: Collect and/or compile research data for greenhouse and field research trials.\u00a0 Help design, develop, implement, and maintain field trials on the research farm and grower fields. Maintain and operate field research equipment. Ensure equipment is in good condition, keep records of maintenance, and operate for field research trials. Provide agronomic management for field trials conducted on the research farm including nutrition, irrigation, and pest management. Ensure compliance with herbicide applications and organic certification and maintain records on all field plots. Prepare reports and data analysis for use in grower reports, extension meetings, and co-author peer-reviewed publications and extension publications (and/or for presentation at scientific symposiums/conferences). Supervise student workers. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in plant sciences, crop science, horticulture, weed science, pest management, biology, natural resources or related field by time of hire. Experience conducting field and laboratory research, including experimental design. Experience with basic statistical analysis of data. Experience with operating and maintaining tractor equipment and field equipment, skilled with power tools, and ability to drive trailers for moving equipment. General knowledge and ability to use computers, including proficiency with information technology, professional office software and collaborative work platforms. Effective communications (written and verbal) skills. Must have or be able to obtain an Oregon Department of Agriculture Pesticide Consultant License with the Demonstration and Research option within six months of employment and maintain it through employment. Must be able to work independently and as part of a group of temporary employees and students. Demonstrable commitment to collaborative and respectful learning and working environments that are safe, inclusive, and welcoming. \u00a0 Ability to learn and adapt to using multiple forms of digital communication systems, including websites, email newsletters, and other tools in a changing technological environment. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. This position requires driving a university vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the university; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a motor vehicle history check, possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions as per University Policy 05-030. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in weed science research Supervisory experience Experience with operating and maintaining tractor equipment Experience in research environment Proficiency with ARM Statistical Software and R Working Conditions/Schedule: \u2022 Field work and greenhouse work include work under field conditions (cold, heat, wet and dust). \u2022 Regular work schedule but may require some overnight travel and work outside of normal working hours (early morning, evening, weekends) if need arises. \u2022 Working with agricultural chemicals \u2022 Working around heavy machinery like tractors and tractor equipment \u2022 Driving is essential to operate a motor vehicle to travel to research sites. \u2022 Ability to carry, lift, push, and pull items weighing up to 50 pounds Salary Range: Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2027-01-11 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Botany---Plant-Pathology--Internal-Employment-Opportunity-_JR0001485": {"title": "Faculty Research Assistant: Botany & Plant Pathology (Internal Employment Opportunity)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nImportant Notifications: Application Deadline: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Current Employees: Do not apply via the OSU Career site. Instead, please login to your regular Workday account and visit the Jobs Hub to apply. Department: Botany & Plant Pathology - Special Instructions to Applicants: This is an Internal Employment Opportunity. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Mana Ohkura Mana.ohkura@oregonstate.edu 541-737-5542 Job Summary: This is an Internal Employment Opportunity. The Department of Botany & Plant Pathology invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 12-month, fixed-term Faculty Research Assistant position.\u00a0Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. The faculty research assistant will work in the OSU Plant Clinic to perform molecular testing on plant diagnostic samples and to perform research to optimize new molecular tests. Key Responsibilities: Perform molecular testing on plant diagnostic samples for pathogens and pests using PCR, qPCR, ELISA, and DNA sequencing. Conduct research to adopt and optimize new molecular tests to increase accuracy and efficiency. Collect and analyze testing data for survey projects. General lab maintenance (washing labware, autoclaving supplies, and organizing records) Qualifications: Required Qualifications: BS in biology or closely related field. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. Preferred Qualifications: At least 1 year of experience performing molecular pathogen testing in a plant diagnostic clinic. Working Conditions/Schedule: This is an on-site position working standard hours in a laboratory setting. Salary Range: Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2027-01-04 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Newport-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Marine-Mammal-Institute-GEMM-Lab_JR0001383": {"title": "Faculty Research Assistant: Marine Mammal Institute-GEMM Lab", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nImportant Notifications: Application Deadline: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Current Employees: Do not apply via the OSU Career site. Instead, please login to your regular Workday account and visit the Jobs Hub to apply. Department: Marine Mammal Institute - Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter detailing qualifications and experience. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0\u00a0 For additional information please contact: Leigh Torres Leigh.torres@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The Marine Mammal Institute invites applications for an hourly or salaried part-time (0.60 FTE), 12-month, fixed-term Faculty Research Assistant position. Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. I am seeking a Faculty Research Assistant to work in my research lab (The GEMM Lab) within the Marine Mammal Institute at Oregon State University based in Newport, Oregon https://mmi.oregonstate.edu/gemm-lab . This position will support multiple aspects of research activities, field operations, and lab management. Key Responsibilities: Operate small boat (e.g., RHIB, Zodiac) around cetaceans for ecological data collection Perform routine maintenance tasks on research vessel, truck, and trailer, and coordinates specialized maintenance and repairs as needed Conduct marine mammal survey observations aboard US Coast Guard helicopters and mid-size and large research vessels Oversight of equipment (cameras, drones, sensors, etc.) maintenance, storage, organization Data management and sample storage/archiving Process and organize photo-ID images Qualifications: Required Qualifications: A bachelor\u2019s degree in the natural sciences with 2 years\u2019 significant research experience Experience as a marine mammal observer Extensive experience as a small boat driver around cetaceans Experience in ecological data collection, including cetacean photo-ID, behavioral observations, prey sampling, drone operations, suction-cup tagging, biopsy Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Clear, honest communication skills Ability to work on collaborative projects with a multidisciplinary team Ability to work independently and creatively within a team environment and maintain a constructive and positive research culture. This position requires driving a university vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the university; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a motor vehicle history check, possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions as per University Policy 05-030. Preferred Qualifications: A Master\u2019s degree in the natural sciences Experience using Microsoft Access, ArcGIS, and/or Matlab Experience using R programming for data wrangling, organization, and visualization and statistical analysis. Record of scientific publication as lead or co-author Experience conducting photo-ID analysis of cetaceans. Demonstrated success of working on several concurrent projects and adapting to shifting priorities and deadlines. Working Conditions/Schedule: This position must be able to work regularly in outdoor environments, including on boats in marine environments. Incumbent must be able to lift heavy objects (>30lbs). Occasional travel and driving for remote fieldwork is expected. Incumbent must have ability and willingness to work occasional long days in the field when the weather is right, which may include weekends and holidays. Salary Range: Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-11-02 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027---Nutrition_JR0001588": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026-2027:  Nutrition", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nApplication Deadline Notification: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Department: School of Nutrition and Public Health Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) Supplemental Questions: (please attach as a separate document) a) Explain your availability to teach face-to-face on-campus courses. b) Explain your availability to teach courses online, and include information about previous experiences and what platforms and software you have used. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Veronica Irvin veronica.irvin@oregonstate.edu 541-737-1074 Job Summary: The School of Nutrition and Public Health in the College of Health invites applications for one or more fixed term, non-tenure track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the School Head. Salary is competitive and will be negotiated with the School Head. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. We passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. Through nationally recognized online degree programs, certificates, and microcredentials offered via OSU Ecampus, we expand access to high-quality education and serve diverse learners wherever they live and work. The School of Nutrition and Public Health at Oregon State University advances knowledge and prepares future professionals through excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement. We foster a collaborative and innovative environment where faculty and students work together to address complex health issues, promote equity, and develop solutions that make a meaningful impact in Oregon, across the nation, and around the world. Key Responsibilities : Teach and administer undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Nutrition. Hold regular office hours to assist students with coursework and answer questions regarding curriculum. May supervise graduate and undergraduate teaching assistants. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master\u2019s degree in Nutrition or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Experience with modern pedagogical techniques. Ability to communicate effectively with a wide variety of audiences verbally and in writing. Evident commitment to inclusive excellence. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: PhD in Nutrition or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Registered Dietitian credential. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Instructor position to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Applications to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-13 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Environmental---Occupational-Health-and-Safety_JR0001587": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026-2027: Environmental & Occupational Health and Safety", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nApplication Deadline Notification: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Department: School of Nutrition and Public Health Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) Supplemental Questions: (please attach as a separate document) a) Explain your availability to teach face-to-face on-campus courses. b) Explain your availability to teach courses online, and include information about previous experiences and what platforms and software you have used. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Veronica Irvin veronica.irvin@oregonstate.edu 541-737-1074 Job Summary: The School of Nutrition and Public Health in the College of Health invites applications for one or more fixed term, non-tenure track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the School Head. Salary is competitive and will be negotiated with the School Head. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. We passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. Through nationally recognized online degree programs, certificates, and microcredentials offered via OSU Ecampus, we expand access to high-quality education and serve diverse learners wherever they live and work. The School of Nutrition and Public Health at Oregon State University advances knowledge and prepares future professionals through excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement. We foster a collaborative and innovative environment where faculty and students work together to address complex health issues, promote equity, and develop solutions that make a meaningful impact in Oregon, across the nation, and around the world. Key Responsibilities : Teach and administer undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Environmental & Occupational Health and Safety. Hold regular office hours to assist students with coursework and answer questions regarding curriculum. May supervise graduate and undergraduate teaching assistants. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master\u2019s degree in Public Health, Environmental Health, Occupational Health, or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Experience with modern pedagogical techniques. Ability to communicate effectively with a wide variety of audiences verbally and in writing. Evident commitment to educational excellence. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: PhD in Public Health or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Instructor position to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Applications to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-13 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Social-Work_JR0001554": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Social Work", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nApplication Deadline Notification: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Department: College of Education Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Daniel Cavanaugh cavanda@oregonstate.edu\u00a0 Job Summary: The College of Education invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-to-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal at the discretion of the Dean. For over a century, Oregon State University has been a leader in the field of education. From our cutting-edge research to our commitments to social justice and lifelong learning, we prepare and empower the next generation of change-makers as teachers, counselors, higher education leaders, and scholars.\u00a0 The purpose of this position is to develop and/or deliver courses for the College of Education\u2019s Social Work programs. Courses are fully online in undergraduate programs.This position is directly responsible to advance the missions of the College of Education in the Social Work Major. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and/or teach courses within the Social Work major programs. Courses are expected to promote experiential learning and success of students from diverse backgrounds. Align andragogical practices with principles and practices identified in the OSU Quality Teaching Framework. and be evaluated based on the ability to achieve equitable learning outcomes. Participate in necessary training and meetings to develop, maintain, and teach with appropriate technologies in OSU\u2019s learning management system (Canvas). Participate in necessary training and meetings to teach in any CORE Education course where instruction is assigned. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Earned Master\u2019s degree in Social Work or a closely related field.\u00a0 Documented experience teaching, training, or facilitating learning or developing curriculum in the course content area.\u00a0 Record of work with underrepresented/underserved students or other audiences. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS : Doctorate degree in Social Work or a closely related field for any course level.\u00a0 Two years of documented social work practice post-degree\u00a0 Experience developing and/or teaching courses using online and virtual technologies and formats.\u00a0 Teaching experience at the college or university level.\u00a0 Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners.\u00a0 Working Conditions/Schedule: This position is fully remote, allowing the employee to work from anywhere within the United States. There is no requirement for physical presence at a specific location, providing flexibility to choose a residence that best suits personal and professional needs. The role supports a distributed work environment, leveraging digital communication and collaboration tools to ensure seamless connectivity and productivity across different time zones. Candidates should have reliable internet access and be able to maintain regular working hours aligned with the team but otherwise have the freedom to work from any U.S. location. Office space may be provided in Furman Hall at OSU\u2019s Corvallis campus. Classes meet online. Virtual attendance at quarterly faculty meetings may be required. Virtual meetings with supervisor are required. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-12 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Health-Management---Policy_JR0001569-1": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Health Management & Policy", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nDepartment: School of Nutrition and Public Health Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) Supplemental Questions: (please attach as a separate document) a) Explain your availability to teach face-to-face on-campus courses. b) Explain your availability to teach courses online, and include information about previous experiences and what platforms and software you have used. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Veronica Irvin veronica.irvin@oregonstate.edu 541-737-1074 Job Summary: The School of Nutrition and Public Health in the College of Health invites applications for one or more fixed term, non-tenure track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the School Head. Salary is competitive and will be negotiated with the School Head. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. We passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. Through nationally recognized online degree programs, certificates, and microcredentials offered via OSU Ecampus, we expand access to high-quality education and serve diverse learners wherever they live and work. The School of Nutrition and Public Health at Oregon State University advances knowledge and prepares future professionals through excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement. We foster a collaborative and innovative environment where faculty and students work together to address complex health issues, promote equity, and develop solutions that make a meaningful impact in Oregon, across the nation, and around the world. Key Responsibilities : Teach and administer undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Health Management & Policy. Hold regular office hours to assist students with coursework and answer questions regarding curriculum. May supervise graduate and undergraduate teaching assistants. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master\u2019s degree in Public Health, Health Management & Policy or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Experience with modern pedagogical techniques. Ability to communicate effectively with a wide variety of audiences verbally and in writing. Evident commitment to educational excellence. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: PhD in Public Health or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Instructor position to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Applications to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-12 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool----2026-2027--Health-Promotion---Behavior_JR0001555": {"title": "Instructor Pool -  2026/2027: Health Promotion & Behavior", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nDepartment: School of Nutrition and Public Health Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) Supplemental Questions: (please attach as a separate document) a) Explain your availability to teach face-to-face on-campus courses. b) Explain your availability to teach courses online, and include information about previous experiences and what platforms and software you have used. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Veronica Irvin veronica.irvin@oregonstate.edu 541-737-1074 Job Summary: The School of Nutrition and Public Health in the College of Health invites applications for one or more fixed term, non-tenure track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the School Head. Salary is competitive and will be negotiated with the School Head. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. We passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. Through nationally recognized online degree programs, certificates, and microcredentials offered via OSU Ecampus, we expand access to high-quality education and serve diverse learners wherever they live and work. The School of Nutrition and Public Health at Oregon State University advances knowledge and prepares future professionals through excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement. We foster a collaborative and innovative environment where faculty and students work together to address complex health issues, promote equity, and develop solutions that make a meaningful impact in Oregon, across the nation, and around the world. Key Responsibilities : Teach and administer undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Health Promotion and Health Behavior. Hold regular office hours to assist students with coursework and answer questions regarding curriculum. May supervise graduate and undergraduate teaching assistants. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master\u2019s degree in Public Health, Health Promotion & Health Behavior, or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Experience with modern pedagogical techniques. Ability to communicate effectively with a wide variety of audiences verbally and in writing. Evident commitment to educational excellence. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: PhD in Public Health or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Instructor position to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Applications to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-09 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Global-Health_JR0001553": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Global Health", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nDepartment: School of Nutrition and Public Health Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) Supplemental Questions: (please attach as a separate document) a) Explain your availability to teach face-to-face on-campus courses. b) Explain your availability to teach courses online, and include information about previous experiences and what platforms and software you have used. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Veronica Irvin veronica.irvin@oregonstate.edu 541-737-1074 Job Summary: The School of Nutrition and Public Health in the College of Health invites applications for one or more fixed term, non-tenure track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the School Head. Salary is competitive and will be negotiated with the School Head. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. We passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. Through nationally recognized online degree programs, certificates, and microcredentials offered via OSU E-campus, we expand access to high-quality education and serve diverse learners wherever they live and work. The School of Nutrition and Public Health at Oregon State University advances knowledge and prepares future professionals through excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement. We foster a collaborative and innovative environment where faculty and students work together to address complex health issues, promote equity, and develop solutions that make a meaningful impact in Oregon, across the nation, and around the world. Key Responsibilities: Teach and administer undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Global Health. Hold regular office hours to assist students with coursework and answer questions regarding curriculum. May supervise graduate and undergraduate teaching assistants. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master\u2019s degree in Public Health, Global Health, or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Experience with modern pedagogical techniques. Ability to communicate effectively with a wide variety of audiences verbally and in writing. Evident commitment to educational excellence. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: PhD in Public Health or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Instructor position to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Applications to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-09 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor_JR0001433": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nDepartment: College of Science Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 30, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) A Statement of Research 4) Statement of Teaching Letters of Reference will be requested for those advanced to the reference stage. At that time, you will be asked to provide contact information for your referees who will be sent a secure quicklink that will allow them to upload the requested letters of reference on your behalf. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Juan Vanegas at Vanegasj@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-7800. Job Summary: The Department of Biochemistry and Biophysics in the College of Science at Oregon State University invites applications for a full-time, (1.00 FTE) 9-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Biochemistry and Biophysics position beginning September 2027. The Department of Biochemistry and Biophysics at Oregon State University seeks an innovative and collaborative scientist to join a dynamic research community dedicated to advancing discovery across multiple scales of biology, from atomic-resolution studies of biomolecular structure and dynamics to cellular, physiological, and organismal biology. This position offers a unique opportunity to establish and grow a cutting-edge research program within a highly interdisciplinary environment that fosters collaboration across biochemistry, biophysics, molecular biology, neuroscience, and related fields. Candidates will have access to exceptional institutional resources, including advanced NMR spectroscopy, cryo-electron microscopy sample preparation and national cryo-EM facilities, X-ray crystallography infrastructure, robust molecular biology and protein biochemistry support, state-of-the-art electrophysiology systems, and emerging AI-enabled computational resources through the Jen-Hsun & Lori Huang Collaborative Innovation Complex. The department also offers outstanding opportunities for graduate student recruitment and training through the NIH-supported T32 Predoctoral Molecular Biophysics Training Grant and the internationally recognized NIH-funded GCE4All Center. \u00a0 The successful candidate will contribute to Oregon State University's mission through excellence in research, teaching, mentoring, and service. Responsibilities include developing and maintaining a nationally recognized research program, teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in areas such as biochemistry, biophysics, molecular biology, and neuroscience, and creating innovative coursework aligned with their expertise, including online instructional offerings. The faculty member will mentor undergraduate researchers, graduate students, and postdoctoral scholars while fostering an inclusive, supportive, and collaborative research environment. Candidates will have the opportunity to play a key role in the continued growth of the university's neuroscience initiatives and interdisciplinary training programs, helping to prepare the next generation of scientists through outstanding education, mentorship, and scholarly leadership. Key Duties: Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses to support our programs in biochemistry, biophysics, molecular biology, and neuroscience. Developing advanced undergraduate and graduate courses aligned with the candidate's area of expertise, including coursework amenable to online asynchronous delivery. Contributing to the continued growth and success of Oregon State University's neuroscience programs, including the university's recent effort in developing an online undergraduate degree in Neuroscience. Implementing evidence-based and student-centered teaching practices that support student engagement and success across residential and online learning environments. Mentoring undergraduate researchers, graduate students, and postdoctoral scholars. Participating in graduate education and interdisciplinary training programs, including opportunities associated with the NIH T32 Predoctoral Molecular Biophysics Training Grant. Fostering an inclusive, supportive, and collaborative research environment that promotes scientific excellence and professional development. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent degree in Biochemistry, Biophysics, Neuroscience, Molecular Biology, or a closely related field. Demonstrated record of research achievement in a Neuroscience-related field, and potential to develop an internationally recognized, externally funded research program. A demonstrated commitment to equity and inclusion including a commitment to education equity and to advancing the participation of all individuals in science. A demonstrated ability or significant potential for teaching excellence and commitment to student success which can benefit the graduate and undergraduate programs of the College of Science, including serving online students in the planned Neuroscience undergraduate degree. A demonstrated ability or significant potential for mentoring undergraduate students, graduate students, and postdoctoral scholars. Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral or equivalent research experience. Research that complements existing departmental strengths in structural biology, molecular biophysics, chemical biology, neuroscience, bioinformatics, molecular modelling, or genetic code expansion. Experience with advanced biophysical, structural, computational, or molecular approaches relevant to neuroscience. Research approaches that support the education and mentoring of remote online undergraduate students. Working Conditions/Schedule: Schedule as needed to perform duties, may include some evenings, nights, and weekends. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2027-09-07 Anticipated End Date: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Counselor-Education_JR0001509-1": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Counselor Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Education Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum VItae; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Abraham Cazares-Cervantes cazaresa@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The College of Education invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-to-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal at the discretion of the Dean. \u00a0 Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. \u00a0 For over a century, Oregon State University has been a leader in the field of education. From our cutting-edge research to our commitments to social justice and lifelong learning, we prepare and empower the next generation of change-makers as teachers, counselors, higher education leaders, and scholars.\u00a0 The purpose of this position is to develop and/or deliver courses for the College of Education\u2019s Counseling programs. Courses may be hybrid or fully online in undergraduate or graduate programs.\u00a0This position is directly responsible to advance the missions of the College of Education in the Counseling Major.\u00a0 Key Responsibilities: Develop and/or teach courses within the Counseling major programs.\u00a0 Participate in necessary training and meetings to develop, maintain, and teach with appropriate technologies in OSU\u2019s learning management system (Canvas).\u00a0 Courses are expected to promote experimental learning and success of students from varied backgrounds.\u00a0 Qualifications: Required Qualifications:\u00a0\u00a0 Earned Master\u2019s degree in Counseling, Counselor Education, or a closely related field.\u00a0 Earned Doctorate degree in Counseling, Counselor Education, or a closely related field.\u00a0 Documented experience teaching, training, or facilitating learning or developing curriculum in the course content area.\u00a0 Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners.\u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0\u00a0 Doctorate degree in Counseling, Counselor Education, or a closely related\u00a0 field for any course level.\u00a0 Demonstrable practical or clinical experience in the counseling field.\u00a0 Experience developing and/or teaching courses using blended technologies and formats (e.g. hybrid, online).\u00a0 Teaching experience at the college or university level.\u00a0 Demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence.\u00a0 Working Conditions/Schedule: Shared office space is provided in Furman Hall at OSU\u2019s Corvallis campus. Local travel for class meetings is required. Classes meet online and/or in-person weekly in Wilsonville or Portland, Oregon. Attendance at quarterly faculty meetings may be required. Virtual meetings with supervisor are required Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-07 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Epidemiology_JR0001526": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026-2027: Epidemiology", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nDepartment: School of Nutrition and Public Health Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) Supplemental Questions: (please attach as a separate document) a) Explain your availability to teach face-to-face on-campus courses. b) Explain your availability to teach courses online, and include information about previous experiences and what platforms and software you have used. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Veronica Irvin veronica.irvin@oregonstate.edu 541-737-1074 Job Summary: The School of Nutrition and Public Health in the College of Health invites applications for one or more fixed term, non-tenure track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the School Head. Salary is competitive and will be negotiated with the School Head. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. We passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. Through nationally recognized online degree programs, certificates, and microcredentials offered via OSU E-campus, we expand access to high-quality education and serve diverse learners wherever they live and work. The School of Nutrition and Public Health at Oregon State University advances knowledge and prepares future professionals through excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement. We foster a collaborative and innovative environment where faculty and students work together to address complex health issues, promote equity, and develop solutions that make a meaningful impact in Oregon, across the nation, and around the world. Key Responsibilities: Teach and administer undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Epidemiology. Hold regular office hours to assist students with coursework and answer questions regarding curriculum. May supervise graduate and undergraduate teaching assistants. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master\u2019s degree in Public Health, Epidemiology, or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Experience with modern pedagogical techniques. Ability to communicate effectively with a wide variety of audiences verbally and in writing. Evident commitment to educational equity. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: PhD in Public Health or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Instructor position to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Applications to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-08 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor--Extension-Plant-Pathology_JR0001109": {"title": "Assistant Professor: Extension Plant Pathology", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Botany & Plant Pathology Extension Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 6, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter addressing each of the required qualifications. \u00a0 3) Statement of Research 4) Statement of Teaching/Extension \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Joseph Spatafora Joseph.spatafora@oregonstate.edu 5417378134 Job Summary: This is a full-time, 1.0 FTE tenure-track position at Oregon State University in the Department of Botany and Plant Pathology within the College of Agricultural Sciences. This position is funded at 0.75 FTE, and the faculty member is expected to fund the remaining 0.25 FTE through grants and contracts. For the first three years, full funding at 1.0 FTE will be provided by the college. The duties associated with this position are to provide statewide leadership in developing an Extension research program aimed at the diagnosis and management of plant diseases of Oregon\u2019s various fruit, nut and ornamental/nursery industries. Educational efforts are provided to individual growers, field consultants, federal and state employees, Master Gardeners, and OSU faculty. Scholarship activities directly relate to the mission and responsibilities of the Department of Botany and Plant Pathology and include the production of the Pacific Northwest Plant Disease Management Handbook. Service may include activities that contribute to the effectiveness of the department, college, university, and/or professional societies. \u00a0 The Department of Botany and Plant Pathology (BPP) in the College of Agricultural Sciences maintains a cutting-edge research culture with more than 50 Faculty led research programs.\u00a0 The department also delivers contemporary educational programs with more than 40 graduate students and 300 undergraduate students. Major extension and outreach activities of BPP are associated with the OSU Plant Clinic, the OSU Herbarium, and associated Extension faculty. BPP is located on the main Corvallis campus of OSU in the newly renovated Cordley Hall.\u00a0 OSU is the land-grant institution for the state of Oregon with an enrollment of more than 34,000 students, and the College of Agricultural Sciences is the founding college of OSU. Corvallis is located in the heart of the Willamette Valley, approximately 50 miles from the Pacific Ocean and about 75 miles to the Cascade Mountains. It is a vibrant community with excellent K-12 education schools and medical facilities, strong public transportation and biking infrastructure, and local farmers\u2019 markets and agriculture. \u00a0 There is an expectation that, as part of your role in the college, you embody and advance the principles and practices conveyed in the\u00a0 CAS CARE Commitment \u00a0document. \u00a0 Oregon State University\u2019s commitment to student success includes hiring, retaining, and developing diverse faculty to mentor and educate our undergraduate and graduate students from entry through graduation. The Oregon State Plan,\u00a0 Prosperity Widely Shared , exhibits the strategies we believe are critical to advancing and equalizing learner success. The College of Agricultural Sciences is likewise committed to the success of all learners, as evidenced by its extension and outreach programs under our\u00a0 Strategic Advantages . Key Responsibilities: Extension Teaching and Related Assignments Applied Research Scholarship Service Qualifications: Required Qualifications: PhD in Plant Pathology or related field Publication record in, or relevant to, applied plant pathology (field-based, greenhouse, laboratory) Experience in, or potential for, development and delivery of Extension educational programming in plant pathology. Record of, or potential for, collaborative science including outreach to stakeholders. Demonstrable commitment to inclusive excellence. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. \u00a0 This position requires driving a university vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the university; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a motor vehicle history check, possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions as per University Policy 05-030. Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral experience. Quantitative skills, including but not limited to artificial intelligence. Record of, or potential for, successful extramural funding. Record of/commitment to work with underrepresented/underserved students or other audiences. Life experience, education, or training that broadens capacity to equalize student success or impact underserved audiences. Working Conditions/Schedule: \u2022 Office and laboratory in Cordley Hall \u2022 Botany and Pathology Experimental Field Lab \u2022 College of Agricultural Sciences Greenhouses Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-11-30 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--English--Writing--Film--and-Applied-Journalism_JR0001312": {"title": "Instructor Pool \u2013 2026/2027: English, Writing, Film, and Applied Journalism", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Liberal Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed and considered as opportunities arise throughout the 2026/2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) Statement of Teaching (upload as separate document). For additional information please contact: Amanda Bressler Amanda.Bressler@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The School of Writing, Literature, and Film invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-27 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. Instructors may be needed to teach on campus and Ecampus courses in the following areas: Composition, Technical and Professional Writing, Business Writing, Creative Writing, Intro to Literature, Applied Journalism, and English-oriented ESL. As part of the College of Liberal Arts, the School of Writing, Literature, and Film is a community that includes and values the voices of all people. As such, we recognize the social barriers that have systematically marginalized and excluded people and communities based on race, ethnicity, gender, sexual identity, socioeconomic background, age, disability, national origin and religion. We are committed to the equity of opportunities, and strive to promote and advance diverse communities. We value and proactively seek genuine participation from these historically under-represented and underserved groups, and recognize them as an essential component of creating a welcoming and rich academic, intellectual, and cultural environment for everyone. Oregon State is a leading research university located in one of the safest, smartest, greenest, most environmentally responsible small cities in the nation. We are located in Corvallis, situated 90 miles south of Portland, and an hour from the Cascades or the Pacific Coast in the heart of Western Oregon\u2019s Willamette Valley. Founded in 1868, Oregon State is the state\u2019s Land Grant university and is one of only two universities in the U.S. to have Sea Grant, Space Grant and Sun Grant designations. Oregon State is also the only university in Oregon to hold both the Carnegie Foundation\u2019s top designation for research institutions and its prestigious Community Engagement classification. Key Responsibilities: Instruction: Will administer and teach undergraduate courses in the following areas: Composition, Technical and Professional Writing, Business Writing, Creative Writing, Intro to Literature and English-oriented ESL. Instructors may be needed to teach courses during the fall, winter, spring, and/or summer terms. \u00a0 Service: Full-time instructors serve on committees and attend or contribute to professional trainings as needed. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Masters degree in English, Writing, Creative Writing, Journalism, or closely related field Teaching experience at the college or university level. Evident commitment to educational equity. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in English or a closely related field. Substantial experience teaching in multiple writing subjects. Experience developing curriculum for in-person and for Ecampus delivery. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-12-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool--2026-2027--Adult---Higher-Education_JR0001459": {"title": "Instructor Pool -2026/2027: Adult & Higher Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Education Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: 1) A CV; and 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) Statement of Teaching - please attach as a separate document The salary range listed reflects the full-time salary range and will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Kirsten Hextrum kirsten.hextrum@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The College of Education invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-to-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal at the discretion of the Dean. For over a century, Oregon State University has been a leader in the field of education. From our cutting-edge research to our commitments to social justice and lifelong learning, we prepare and empower the next generation of change-makers as teachers, counselors, higher education leaders, and scholars.\u00a0 The purpose of this position is to develop and/or deliver courses for the College of Education\u2019s Adult and Higher Education program. Courses may be hybrid or fully online in undergraduate or graduate programs and graduate certificates. This position is directly responsible to advance the missions of the College of Education and the Adult and Higher Education (AHE) program area. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and/or teach courses within the Adult and Higher Education major and graduate certificate programs. Participate in necessary training and meetings to develop, maintain, and teach with appropriate technologies in OSU\u2019s learning management system (Canvas). Courses are expected to promote experimental learning and success of students from varied backgrounds. Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Earned Master\u2019s degree in Adult and Higher Education or a closely related field Documented experience teaching, training, or facilitating learning or developing curriculum PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS : Earned Doctorate degree in Adult and Higher Education or a closely related field Professional experience specific to the course content area and/or completion of coursework in course content area. Experience developing and/or teaching courses using blended technologies and formats (e.g. hybrid, online). Teaching experience at the college or university level. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Shared Desk space is provided in Furman Hall at OSU\u2019s Corvallis campus if requested. Local travel for the doctoral program is required. Doctoral classes meet in-person twice per term at the OSU Portland Center in Portland, Oregon. Attendance at quarterly faculty meetings is optional. Meetings with supervisors required. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-02 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor--Military-History_JR0001447": {"title": "Instructor: Military History", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nDepartment: School of History, Philosophy, and Religion Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by January 1, 2027. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) Statement of Teaching 4) At the Reference Check stage, please include a list of 3-5 people (with up-to-date contact information) who would be able to provide a professional reference for you. \u00a0 Starting salary will be $59,000-$64,000, based on skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Stacey Smith at Stacey.Smith@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-1258. \u00a0 Job Summary: The Department of History invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 9-month, fixed-term Instructor position.\u00a0Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. Key Responsibilities: Teach lower-division history survey courses, and upper-division and/or graduate courses in Military History, including U.S. Military History, European Military History, American Diplomatic History, and related areas. Develop new courses in related fields. Participate in recruiting and mentoring students, including especially students in the military history minor. Participate in departmental and college governance and professional activities; serve on university committees, as time, interest and aptitude permit. This Instructor role in the School of History, Philosophy, and Religion is a full-time non-tenure track position. The person in this role is intended to have primary expertise in military history or war studies with a preferred emphasis on the United States.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0The Instructor will teach ten courses each academic year (typically 3-3-4).\u00a0Oregon State University (OSU)\u00a0is on the quarter system, with classes of 10 weeks of instruction. The Instructor will be expected to teach a combination of existing upper-level history courses, which may include: American military history before and after 1865, American diplomatic history, the United States and Vietnam, European military history, the experience of war, and the Historian\u2019s Craft (a general methodology course). Duties may also involve teaching lower-division history surveys related to the Instructor\u2019s areas of expertise. The Instructor will have the opportunity to teach graduate students enrolled in upper-division courses and to design new courses that speak to their interests. The teaching load will include a combination of synchronous in-person courses on the Corvallis campus and asynchronous courses on OSU\u2019s vibrant and highly ranked Ecampus. Additional information about curriculum can be\u00a0 found here .\u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Liberal Arts is a community that includes and values the voices of all people.\u00a0 As such, we recognize the social barriers that have systematically marginalized and excluded people and communities based on race, ethnicity, gender, sexual identity, socioeconomic background, age, disability, national origin and religion. We are committed to the equity of opportunities, and strive to promote and advance diverse communities. We value and proactively seek genuine participation from these historically under-represented and underserved groups, and recognize them as an essential component of creating a welcoming and rich academic, intellectual, and cultural environment for everyone. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: PhD in History or closely related field (by time of position start.) Demonstrated ability to teach courses at the college/university level in military history, war studies, or closely related fields. Record of teaching practices that align with OSU Quality Teaching Framework. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise in military history, war studies, or related field. Experience developing and teaching asynchronous distance education courses. Experience with outreach and engagement, such as participating in events connecting history to contemporary issues. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: $55,000 - $64,000 Anticipated Start Date: 2027-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2028-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor--tenure-track-_JR0001129": {"title": "Assistant Professor (tenure-track)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nDepartment: College of Agricultural Sciences | Agricultural Education, Communication & Sciences Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents:\u00a0 \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position.\u00a0 3) Statement of Research 4) Statement of Teaching 5) Transcripts \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience.\u00a0 \u00a0 For additional information please contact:\u00a0 Taylor Foerster taylor.foerster@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The College of Agricultural Sciences | Agricultural Education, Communication & Sciences invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 9-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor position. The incumbent in this position will focus on providing innovative development and instruction in Agriculture and Natural Resources Communication. The individual will teach, recruit, develop curriculum, and mentor undergraduate and graduate students, conduct a nationally recognized research and scholarly program and engage in service activities that further the growth of our Agricultural Education, Communication, and Sciences Department. This person will be helping develop curriculum for an agricultural and natural resources communication undergraduate major for both in-person and on Ecampus. This person will collaborate with faculty in the department and other colleges on research, teaching, and curriculum development. \u00a0 All Oregon State University faculty in the professorial ranks have a responsibility to engage in scholarship and creative activity. Scholarship is intellectual work in research, teaching, or extension that is shared with peers in journals, in formal peer-reviewed presentations at professional meetings, or comparable peer-evaluated forums. \u00a0 The position will support the university, College of Agricultural Sciences, and department of Agricultural Education, Communication, and Sciences strategic plans. \u00a0 College of Agricultural Sciences faculty are committed to enhancing student success by engaging students in quality academic, research, internships, global studies, and other experiential learning opportunities. Positions with primary responsibility for extension and outreach are likewise committed to learner success through programming appropriate for diverse audiences. There is an expectation that, as part of your role in the college, you embody and advance the principles and practices conveyed in the CAS CARE Commitment document. \u00a0 This position carries the general and specific responsibilities of a faculty member described in the Faculty Handbook and the promotion and tenure guidelines of Oregon State University. These include effective research and extension programs, demonstrable scholarship and creative activity, service contributions, and active professional development. Key Responsibilitie s Teach and create curriculum for undergraduate and graduate coursework within the department specific to Agricultural and Natural Resource Communications Design and conduct research and scholarship leading to new knowledge related to Agricultural and Natural Resource Communications Actively seek extramural grants and contracts supporting research and areas of focus within the department. Provide service to the department, college, university, industry, and profession through committee service and leadership as appropriate and requested by the department, college and university administration. \u00a0 Qualifications: Required Qualifications: A doctorate degree in agricultural communications, communication(s), life science communications, mass communications, journalism, or closely related field. Evidence of successful teaching experience in agricultural communications or natural resources communication, OR successful teaching experience in other fields of communication with expertise in science, including science communication, mass communication, life science communication, or journalism. Evidence of a successful publication record commensurate with the expectations of a tenure-track position. Demonstrated success and commitment to effective teaching. Demonstrated success and commitment to research in agricultural, natural resources, and science communication contexts. Demonstrated success and commitment to scholarship. Demonstrated success and commitment to service. Commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence and ensuring that all individuals have the opportunity to flourish. Demonstrated skills in verbal and written communication. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months . Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise in digital communications (social media, digital media, photography, etc.) Demonstrated ability to innovate, develop, and implement new programs. Demonstrated success in undergraduate and graduate student advising. Demonstrated ability to work with a variety of types of learners in diverse settings, such as online education, continuing professional development, et cetera. Life experience, education, or training that broadens capacity to equalize student success or impact underserved communities. Demonstrated ability to collaborate with local, state, and national stakeholders. Experience with working in the Adobe Suite. Demonstrated experience, knowledge, or interest in engaging with agricultural industries, organizations, and communities, with a willingness to develop and maintain relationships with agricultural stakeholders. Research experience or demonstrated interest in communication related to rural mental health, agricultural health and well-being, or other issues affecting rural and agricultural communities. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: $75,000 - $90,000 Anticipated Start Date: 2027-03-29 Anticipated End Date: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Clinical----Anesthesiology_JR0001331": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor (Clinical):  Anesthesiology", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Veterinary Clinical Sciences Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 28, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Dr. Chris Cebra chris.cebra@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences in the Carlson College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 12-month, fixed-term Assistant or Associate Professor (Clinical): Anesthesiology position. Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. Appointment at the Assistant Professor (Clinical) rank is anticipated; however, appointment at a promoted rank may be considered depending upon the qualifications of the successful candidate. The Carlson College of Veterinary Medicine provides professional and graduate programs for veterinary students leading to DVM, MS and PhD degrees, operates both a Large and a Small Animal Teaching Hospital (VTH), and a State Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory. The College operates within a total budget (from all sources) of approximately $37 million annually, which supports educational programs, veterinary medical and diagnostic public services, and research programs with broad impacts related to animal and human health. The Department of Clinical Sciences oversees clinical, classroom, and laboratory teaching, and scholarly activity of clinical faculty and residents. The VTH provides primary and referral health care for animals throughout the Pacific Northwest. \u00a0 The purpose of this position is to provide clinical service, foster critical thinking, generate original medical information and advance professional veterinary students\u2019 and house officers\u2019 knowledge and skills through research, mentorship and instruction in the Department of Clinical Sciences and the Veterinary Teaching Hospital. The Department is receptive to faculty members seeking part-time appointments. Duties and expectations will vary with the FTE of the appointment. The incumbent provides Anesthesiology services to small and large animal veterinary patients admitted during regular hours and after hours. The incumbent also mentors, assists and instructs interns, fellows, residents, technicians and students in the classroom, teaching laboratory and hospital. The distribution of efforts may change with program needs. \u00a0 Achievement in scholarship and creative activity that is recognized as contributing to the body of knowledge in the practice discipline is required. Such activity should be validated by peers and show evidence of financial independence from university funding, if such funding is required to meet scholarly goals. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES : Clinical Teaching and Service Mentorship, Classroom and Laboratory Instruction Institutional Service and Citizenship Scholarly Activity Qualifications: Required Qualifications (Assistant Professor - Clinical) DVM or equivalent degree. Completed anesthesiology residency training in a program certified by the American College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (ACVAA) or European College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (ECVAA) and qualified to sit for the ACVAA/ECVAA certifying examination. Three years of clinical experience in veterinary anesthesiology, including time spent during residency training, and evidence of some classroom/clinical teaching experience. Excellent patient care and communication skills. Demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence. \u00a0 This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. \u00a0 Required Qualifications (Associate Professor - Clinical) DVM or equivalent degree. Board certification by the ACVAA/ECVAA. Ten years of clinical experience in veterinary anesthesiology, including time spent during residency training, and evidence of some classroom/clinical teaching experience. Candidate should meet the OSU teaching, advising, research and service criteria for appointment at the desired ranks (see the OSU Faculty Handbook for details).\u00a0 OSU will consider previous years of experience at other, similar institutions towards timelines for rank promotions. Excellent patient care and communication skills. Demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence. \u00a0 This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. Preferred Qualifications: Board certification by the ACVAA/ECVAA. Experience in research related to clinical medicine. Experience with dogs, cats, horses, ruminants, camelids and swine; experience with \u201cpocket pets\u201d and \u201cexotic\u201d species is desirable. Demonstrated experience and potential in teaching. Working Conditions/Schedule: Position works non-routine hours, primarily in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2027-01-01 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/CEOAS-Instructor-Pool--2026-2027_JR0001015": {"title": "CEOAS Instructor Pool- 2026/2027", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\n\nDepartment: College of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Sciences Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) A Statement of Teaching. 4) Upload your response to the supplemental question as a separate document: Please describe your prior teaching experience in higher education, including institution and courses taught, mode of delivery (in person, online, lab, field, etc), number of students enrolled, and your role in the course (instructor of record, teaching assistant, etc). Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Kaplan Yalcin at Kaplan.Yalcin@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-1230. Job Summary: The College of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Sciences in Corvallis, Oregon, invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track full/part-time Instructor/Senior Instructor I positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Appointment at the Instructor rank is anticipated; however, appointment at a promoted rank may be considered depending upon the qualifications of the successful candidate. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Assistant Dean for Undergraduate Programs. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. The primary purpose of these positions is to instruct on a term-by-term basis. Instructors may be needed to teach courses, either on-campus or Ecampus, in the following areas: Earth Sciences, Environmental Sciences, Climate Science, Geography, Geology, Geographic Information Sciences, Marine Resource Management, and Ocean and Atmospheric Sciences. Applications may be considered throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Key Responsibilities: D eliver instruction Assess student learning Assign student grades Collaborate with other faculty and program directors Manage graduate teaching assistants and/or undergraduate learning assistants Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Instructor Rank: Master of Arts (MA)/Master of Science (MS) in discipline central to Earth or Environmental Sciences such as Atmospheric Sciences, Environmental Sciences, Geology, Geography, Oceanography of fields relevant to the course being taught. Evidence of or commitment to excellence in inclusive teaching and student success. \u00a0 Senior Instructor I Rank: PhD in Geology, Geography, Geospatial Science, Oceanography, Atmospheric Sciences, Environmental sciences, or a closely-related field. Four years (full time equivalent) of professional experience teaching at the college or university level. Sustained record of exceptional teaching at the college or university level as evidenced by student evaluations of teaching. Preferred Qualifications: All Ranks: Demonstrated ability to teach across modalities, including online courses, and proficiency with online teaching platforms such as Canvas. Instructor Rank: Vision for incorporating high impact pedagogical practices into course design and teaching, including but not limited to experiential learning, community-engaged teaching, inquiry-based learning, and career integration. Senior Instructor I Rank: Demonstrated experience incorporating high impact pedagogical practices course design and teaching, including but not limited to experiential learning, community-engaged teaching, inquiry-based learning, and career integration. Working Conditions/Schedule: This position is located onsite in Corvallis, OR. The incumbent may work remotely as agreed upon with the supervisor, but is expected to be available for on-campus (face to face) teaching assignments and is required to hold on-campus office hours when teaching on-campus classes. Salary Range: Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Graduate-Education_JR0001260": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Graduate Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Office of Graduate Education Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) A Statement of Teaching Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Mo Childers at Mo.Childers@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-2033. Job Summary: The Office of Graduate Education, at\u00a0OSU in Corvallis, Oregon, invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track part-time (typically less than .30 FTE) Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year and Fall Term 2026. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Dean of Academic Affairs. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted \u00a0when positions become available. Key Responsibilities: Deliver instruction Assess student learning Assign student grades Collaborate with other faculty and program director Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree from an accredited institution. Teaching experience at the college/university level aligned with one or more academic course offerings from the Office of Graduate Education. Evident commitment to educational equity. Preferred Qualifications: PhD or terminal degree from an accredited institution. Graduate teaching experience at the college/university level aligned with one or more academic course offerings from the Office of Graduate Education. Working Conditions/Schedule: These positions will be in the classroom (in person on main campus or Ecampus) as needed to instruct courses offered by the Office of Graduate Education. Salary Range: Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: Anticipated End Date: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Chemistry_JR0001354": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor: Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nDepartment: College of Science Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, we must receive applications by November 15, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date until we have a sufficient applicant pool or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. \u00a0 When applying, you will be required to attach the following documents: \u00a0 1) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position (Cover Letter; up to 2 pages).\u00a0 Also, within the cover letter, candidates should express their philosophy of open-mindedness for diverse ideas within the academy, including those different from one\u2019s own, and a commitment to free inquiry based on evidence. \u00a0 2) Curriculum vitae \u00a0 3) Statement of Research: Description of research interests and plans (up to 6 pages). \u00a0 4) Statement of Teaching: A statement of teaching philosophy and instructional experience (not to exceed 2 pages). \u00a0 Letters of Reference will be requested for those advanced to the reference stage. At that time, you will be asked to provide contact information for your referees who will be sent a secure quicklink that will allow them to upload the requested letters of reference on your behalf. \u00a0 For additional information, please contact: Paula Christie at 541-737-1681 or paula.christie@oregonstate.edu or the Search Committee Chair: Prof. Kyriakos Stylianou, kyriakos.stylianou@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The College of Science invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 9-month, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position (depending on qualifications). Any hiring at the rank of Associate Professor with indefinite tenure will be subject to a successful out-of-cycle tenure review process: https://academicaffairs.oregonstate.edu/resources-policies-legislation/policies-and-resources/promotion-and-tenure-guidelines/out-cycle The incumbent will develop an internationally recognized and innovative research program in Physical Chemistry, encompassing experimental, computational, or integrated experimental\u2013computational approaches. The search is broad, with particular interest in molecular and materials theory, spectroscopy, photochemistry and excited-state dynamics, chemical dynamics, statistical mechanics, interfaces and condensed phases, quantum chemistry, quantum materials and quantum computing, semiconductor and energy materials, data-driven chemistry, and AI/ML-enabled chemical and materials discovery. Candidates developing new experimental methodologies or integrating advanced experiments with theory, computation, and data science are especially encouraged. \u00a0 The position represents a strategic opportunity to connect fundamental Physical Chemistry with major research investments at Oregon State University and across Oregon. The successful candidate will have opportunities to engage with the NSF-funded Frontiers of Advanced Semiconductor Technology (FAST) Regional Innovation Engine, led by OSU and involving nearly 100 academic, industry, government, and community partners. Research addressing the fundamental understanding, prediction, characterization, or discovery of semiconductors, electronic and quantum materials, interfaces, energy technologies, and materials relevant to advanced manufacturing will have particularly strong opportunities for engagement. \u00a0 The position will also benefit from OSU\u2019s rapidly expanding capabilities in high-performance computing, artificial intelligence, machine learning, and data-intensive research, including the Jen-Hsun Huang and Lori Mills Huang Collaborative Innovation Complex (HCIC). These investments provide opportunities for research in electronic-structure theory, molecular simulation, computational spectroscopy, quantum chemistry, materials modeling, AI-guided discovery, digital twins, and other computationally intensive areas. They also create an environment in which experimental researchers can closely integrate laboratory discovery with computation, automation, and data science. \u00a0 Experimental candidates will have access to substantial infrastructure across OSU, including advanced capabilities in NMR, mass spectrometry, X-ray diffraction, molecular and materials spectroscopy, and materials characterization, complemented by strengths in molecular and materials synthesis. These resources provide a strong foundation for research spanning ultrafast and molecular spectroscopy, light\u2013matter interactions, quantum phenomena, photochemistry, interfaces, energy conversion, and structure\u2013property relationships in functional materials. \u00a0 The successful candidate will establish an externally funded research program, develop interdisciplinary collaborations, mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers, contribute to teaching in Physical Chemistry and related areas, and participate in the research and educational mission of the Department, College of Science, and University. \u00a0 The successful candidate will join a highly interdisciplinary environment with opportunities for collaboration across Chemistry, Physics, Biochemistry & Biophysics, Mathematics and Statistics, Engineering, Pharmacy, and other units across OSU. Particularly attractive opportunities exist at the intersections of physical chemistry with materials discovery, semiconductor science, quantum materials and quantum computing, spectroscopy and molecular dynamics, photochemistry, energy conversion, interfaces, computational chemistry, AI/ML, and high-performance computing. \u00a0 Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the Department of Chemistry, and typical teaching expectations are currently three 3-4 credit courses per year. Create course design, composition of the course syllabus, selection of text and other supporting materials. Determine topics and subject matter, fashion presentations, creating assessment tools, and overseeing graduate teaching assistants, assigning grades. Instruction methods must follow best practices for diversity, equity, justice, and inclusion. Compliance with University academic regulations is required/essential. Conduct research in the area of specialization so that it attracts national and international recognition and establishes the employee's reputation for scholarly excellence. Expected activities include, but are not limited to, supervision of students and postdoctoral associates in the execution of research; publication of non-refereed papers, web publications, books, book chapters; filing patent applications; submission of grant proposals and administration of successful grants; compliance with University regulatory policies concerning grants and research. Participate in department, College and University Committees. Participate in training/professional development to maintain current knowledge of best practices in teaching, mentoring, and interacting with students. Participation in peer review activities, promotion of the profession through outreach and participation in professional societies. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in Chemistry or an allied discipline. Demonstrable ability or significant potential to conduct high-quality scientific research and support OSU\u2019s strategic plan, \u201cProsperity Widely Shared\u201d. Demonstrable ability to disseminate the results of scholarly activities via scientific publications and conference presentations. Demonstrable ability or significant potential for teaching excellence and commitment to student success that benefits the graduate and undergraduate programs of the Department of Chemistry in the College of Science as well as OSU students as a whole.\u00a0 Demonstrable ability or significant potential for mentoring undergraduate students, graduate students, postdoctoral scholars, and research assistants.\u00a0 A demonstrated commitment to educational equity and to advancing the participation of all individuals\u00a0in science. \u00a0 For appointment at the Associate Professor rank , candidates must additionally demonstrate; an established record of independent scholarship and research productivity, a strong record of securing external research funding, demonstrated excellence in teaching and mentoring, and a record of professional and institutional service commensurate with appointment at the Associate Professor level. Candidates are expected to have demonstrated national or international recognition in their field and meet the standards for appointment at the Associate Professor rank. \u00a0 This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. Preferred Qualifications: Relevant postdoctoral experience. Teaching experience in physical chemistry that extends beyond the duties typically assigned to Graduate Teaching Assistants (e.g., generating course syllabi and/or lecture materials, providing lecture room instruction, instruction to summer camp attendees, etc.). Demonstrable proficiency or significant potential to obtain external research funding. Demonstrable interest in transdisciplinary communication and collaboration, including the potential for engagement in synergistic interactions with other faculty at or outside OSU.\u00a0 Demonstrable interest in outreach and engagement with members of the general public. Working Conditions/Schedule: Schedule as needed to perform duties, may include some evenings, nights and/or weekends. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2027-09-16 Anticipated End Date: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Senior-Instructor-1--Healthcare-Administration_JR0000205": {"title": "Instructor/Senior Instructor 1: Healthcare Administration", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nDepartment: School of Nutrition and Public Health Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) Statement of Teaching Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Veronica Irvin Veronica.Irvin@oregonstate.edu 541-737-8784 Job Summary: The School of Nutrition and Public Health invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 12-month, fixed-term, Instructor/Senior Instructor I position. Reappointment is at the discretion of the School Head. Appointment at the Instructor rank is anticipated; however, appointment at a promoted rank may be considered depending upon the qualifications of the successful candidate. We passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. Through nationally recognized online degree programs, certificates, and microcredentials offered via OSU Ecampus, we expand access to high-quality education and serve diverse learners wherever they live and work. The School of Nutrition and Public Health at Oregon State University advances knowledge and prepares future professionals through excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement. We foster a collaborative and innovative environment where faculty and students work together to address complex health issues, promote equity, and develop solutions that make a meaningful impact in Oregon, across the nation, and around the world. Key Responsibilities: Teaching and other assigned duties Service Qualifications: Required Qualifications for rank of Instructor and Senior Instructor I: Master\u2019s degree in Healthcare Administration or related field Experience teaching online courses and supervising applied projects A demonstrable commitment to inclusive excellence and ability to work collaboratively across disciplines. Ability to work on campus as this position cannot be performed remotely. Additional Qualifications for the Rank of Senior Instructor I: Sustained record of exceptional teaching, advising and service, at the college or university level, as evidenced by student evaluations of teaching. Experience in course development. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Healthcare Administration or related field Experience with accreditation or assessment activities Experience with CAHME and NCHL competencies Working Conditions/Schedule: Work is done in an office environment. Typical schedule is 9-5pm. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2027-07-01 Anticipated End Date: 2028-06-30 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Chemistry_JR0000827": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Science Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed and considered as opportunities arise throughout the 2026/2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Paula Christie Paula.christie@oregonstate.edu 541-737-1681 Job Summary: The Department of Chemistry invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track, full/part-time, Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Department Chair. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. Instructors may be needed to teach courses, either on-campus or Ecampus, in the following areas: analytical, biological, bio-organic, general, environmental, materials, nuclear, Organic, and physical chemistry. The\u00a0OSU \u00a0Department of Chemistry plays a central role in the University's educational, research, and outreach missions, delivering nearly 100,000 student credit hours of instruction annually while maintaining a vibrant graduate program with approximately 100 PhD students. The Department conducts cutting-edge research and scholarly activities focused on all areas of chemistry important to biology, materials, and the environment, including analytical, biological, bio-organic, environmental, materials, nuclear, and physical chemistry. This dynamic setting is ideally suited for nurturing and supporting instructional faculty in their efforts to support the Department\u2019s educational mission, which impacts over 10,000 students each year. The College of Science provides a core instructional role at\u00a0OSU , supporting the ideals of learning, discovery, and engagement that are the foundation of a land-grant university. The College embraces instruction and research in disciplines ranging from the physical, mathematical, and statistical sciences to the life sciences, grounded in unbiased inquiry and a dedication to discovery and innovation. The College of Science is committed to partnering with industry and public agencies to address some of the most compelling challenges of today and tomorrow. Key Responsibilities: Instruction Administer and teach up to 4 on campus or ecampus (training prior to teaching will be provided and is required) undergraduate courses Hold regular Office hours to assist students with coursework and answer questions regarding the curriculum Provide supervision/lead work for up to 5 Graduate or Undergraduate student employees Following college practices on early warnings, student feedbacks, and grading policies Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in Chemistry or a closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Teaching experience at the college and/or university level. An evident commitment to educational equity. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. Preferred Requirements: Ph.D. in Chemistry or a closely related discipline to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-27--Individual-Music-Lessons_JR0000805": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/27: Individual Music Lessons", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Liberal Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed and considered as opportunities arise throughout the 2026/2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Coleen Keedah Coleen.keedah@oregonstate.edu 541-737-5003 Job Summary: The Music program in the School of Visual, Performing, and Design Arts invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track, part-time, 12-month, hourly Instructor positions to teach individual music lessons throughout the 2026-2027 academic year as opportunities become available. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. The primary mission of the Music program at OSU is to provide undergraduate education. Students may seek BA, BS, BM degrees in music as well as a music minor. Key Responsibilities: Instructors may be needed to teach individual, one-on-one music lessons to undergraduate and graduate students. Lesson instruction may be needed for voice, piano, guitar, or a variety of instruments associated with band or orchestra. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Bachelors degree in Music, and/or equivalent professional experience with demonstrated ability to teach at the college level. In order to receive consideration for professional experience, applicants must have demonstrated successful teaching of post-secondary students and attained success with experience in the following areas: Knowledge of repertoire appropriate for post-secondary students in their area of expertise. Professional experience as a performer on their major instrument over a period of not less than 3 years on a regional or national level. Understanding of the pedagogical practices particular to their instrument. Regional reputation as teacher and/or performer. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. Preferred Qualifications: Masters degree in Music, Music Education, the Arts, and/or equivalent professional experience with demonstrated ability to teach at the college level. In order to receive consideration for professional experience, applicants must have demonstrated successful teaching of post-secondary students and attained success with experience in the following areas: Performances with major ensembles and in major venues. Evidence of professional success by former students. Discography and online recordings. Professional reviews in online and print media. History of artistic collaborations with significant performers and conductors. Evidence of innovative pedagogical techniques. Publications of compositions or research in their professional field. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skill, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Theatre-Arts_JR0000802": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Theatre Arts", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Liberal Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed and considered as opportunities arise throughout the 2026/2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Coleen Keedah Coleen.keedah@oregonstate.edu 541-737-5003 Job Summary: The School of Visual, Performing and Design Arts, Department of Theatre, invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026/2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available Instructors may be needed to teach undergraduate courses on campus or through Ecampus in areas of Theatre Arts such as acting, introduction to Theatre Arts, technical theatre, costuming, stage and lighting design, etc. The primary mission of Theatre Arts at OSU is undergraduate education. Students may seek BA and BS degrees in Theatre Arts as well as a Theatre Arts minor. While Theatre Arts, on occasion, participates in the MAIS graduate program, most students in this program are undergraduates. Key Responsibilities: Administer and teach undergraduate courses on campus or through eCampus in areas of Theatre Arts Teach courses such as:\u00a0 acting, introduction to Theatre Arts, technical theatre, costuming, stage and lighting design, etc. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in Theatre Arts or closely related field in-hand by start date. Evident commitment to educational equity. Record of and/or demonstrated interest in engaging, educating, and mentoring a diverse group of learners and enhancing inclusive exellence through teaching, outreach, or programming. Ability to work collegially with other faculty, staff, and students. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience at the college or university level. Record of artistic and/or scholarly achievement in the field. Terminal degree in Theatre or closely related field. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skill, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Graphic-Design_JR0000801": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Graphic Design", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-25\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Liberal Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed and considered as opportunities arise throughout the 2026/2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Coleen Keedah Coleen.keedah@oregonstate.edu 541-737-5003 Job Summary: The School of Visual, Performing and Design Arts (SVPDA), Graphic Design program, invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026/2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. The primary mission of the Graphic Design program at OSU is undergraduate education. Students may seek a Bachelor of Fine Arts degree in graphic design. Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses on-campus or through Ecampus. Possible courses include; typography, design tools & techniques, interaction design, design thinking, information design, branding systems, package design, professional development, design theory, graphic design history, etc. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree with significant industry experience. Record of and/or demonstrated interest in engaging, educating, and mentoring a diverse group of learners and enhancing inclusive excellence through teaching, outreach, or programming. Ability to work collegially with other faculty, staff, and students. Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree Experience teaching at the college level. Evident commitment to educational equity. A demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence. History of success in program/curriculum development. Working Conditions/Schedule: Work schedule may vary depending upon student needs and engagement in campus and/or program activities. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skill, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool--2026-2027--Art---Art-History_JR0000799": {"title": "Instructor Pool- 2026/2027: Art & Art History", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nPart time\n\nDepartment: School of Visual, Performing and Design Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026/2027 academic year as opportunities become available. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Coleen Keedah at Coleen.Keedah@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-5003. Job Summary: The Art and Art History program in the School of Visual, Performing and Design Arts\u00a0at\u00a0OSU in Corvallis, Oregon, invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. The primary mission of the Art and Art History program at OSU is undergraduate education. Students may seek BA/BS degrees in Art (with options in Art History, Studio art as well as Photography and Digital Studio, as well as a BFA degree in in Studio Art or Photography and Digital Studio. An undergraduate minor in Art (options in Studio Art, Photography and Art History) also is offered. Key Responsibilities: Teaching undergraduate courses on-campus or through Ecampus. Courses could be in: film photography, digital photography, photographic processes, documentary photography, studio courses in foundations (2-D, 3-D, drawing), painting, printmaking, screen printing, sculpture, art history, or art appreciation. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Studio courses require: B.F.A., professional experience and applicable teaching experience. Lecture courses require: M.A. or M.F.A. with applicable teaching experience. Record of and/or demonstrated interest in engaging, educating, and mentoring a diverse group of learners and enhancing diversity through teaching, outreach, or programming. Ability to work collegially with other faculty, staff, and students. Preferred Qualifications: For studio courses, M.F.A. For Art History courses, Ph.D. Experience teaching at the college level. Evident commitment to educational equity. A demonstrable commitment to inclusive excellence. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool--2026-2027--Music-Classroom_JR0000804": {"title": "Instructor Pool- 2026/2027: Music Classroom", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nPart time\n\nDepartment: School of Visual, Performing and Design Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026/2027 academic year as opportunities become available. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Coleen Keedah at Coleen.Keedah@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-5003. Job Summary: The Music area in the School of Visual, Performing and Design Arts, invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. The primary mission of the Music program at OSU is undergraduate education. Students may seek BA, BS, and BM degrees in music as well as a music minor. Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses on-campus or through Ecampus. Courses could include: music appreciation, music cultures of the world, aural skills, literature and materials of music, history of music, instrumental techniques, conducting, group piano instruction, music technology, and methods course in music education. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Masters Degree. Demonstrable professional experience with demonstrated ability to teach at the college level. Content knowledge and expertise relevant to the academic area under consideration. Record of and/or demonstrated interest in engaging, educating, and mentoring a diverse group of learners and enhancing inclusive excellence through teaching, outreach, or programming. Ability to work collegially with other faculty, staff, and students. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. Preferred Qualifications: Terminal Degree. Expertise and teaching experience in at least one secondary area, such as composition, performance, music education, or music technology. History of success in program/curriculum development. Working Conditions/Schedule: annual instructor pool posting Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool--2026-2027--Contemporary-Music-Industry_JR0000806": {"title": "Instructor Pool- 2026/2027: Contemporary Music Industry", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nPart time\n\nDepartment: School of Visual, Performing and Design Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026/2027 academic year as opportunities become available. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Coleen Keedah at Coleen.Keedah@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-5003. Job Summary: The Contemporary Music Industry area in the School of Visual, Performing and Design Arts invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026/2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. The primary mission of the Music program at OSU is undergraduate education. Students may seek BA, BS, and BM degrees in music as well as a music minor. Some appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis. Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses through Ecampus. We currently use the Mark Brill Textbook to teach the survey \u00a0 course. Experience in performing, and/or composing music that is centered in the various histories and practices of Latin American traditions, and popularized music forms. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Masters Degree. Demonstrable professional experience with demonstrated ability to teach at the college level. Content knowledge and expertise relevant to the academic area under consideration. Record of and/or demonstrated interest in engaging, educating, and mentoring a diverse group of learners and enhancing inclusive excellence through teaching, outreach, or programming. Ability to work collegially with other faculty, staff, and students. Preferred Qualifications: Terminal Degree. Expertise and teaching experience in at least one secondary area, such as composition/improvisation, 21 st century \u00a0 performance (jazz, pop), or various music software. Familiar with CANVAS software is a plus. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Biological---Ecological-Engineering_JR0000480": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Biological & Ecological Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Biological & Ecological Engineering Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) Please also upload a Statement of Teaching 4) Please attach a list all courses you have the experience to teach and the education/experience you have for that course. See list of BEE courses: https://catalog.oregonstate.edu/courses/bee/ \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information please contact: Jennifer Cohen Jennifer.cohen@oregonstate.edu 541-737-6292 Job Summary: The Department of Biological & Ecological Engineering invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track full/part-time Instructors to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Department Head. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available. Appointment at the Instructor rank is anticipated; however, appointment at a promoted rank may be considered depending upon the qualifications of the successful candidate. The Department of Biological & Ecological Engineering is an academic unit that reports to the College of Agricultural Sciences. The Department is composed of faculty, research assistants, support staff, graduate students, temporary staff and undergraduate students. The mission of Biological & Ecological Engineering is to achieve national and international recognition as a center for excellence for integrated research and education in the pogroms broadly defines as Ecological Engineering, Biological Engineering and Water Resources Engineering, while maintaining strong outreach links to the agricultural and natural resources communities. Our stakeholders will include links to the agricultural and natural resources communities. Our stakeholders will include environmental and ecological consulting firms, ecotechnology providers, entrepreneurial enterprises building new 21st-century biology and ecology based industries, public resource management agencies, and stakeholders in the state with interests in these focus areas. Key Responsibilities: Teach courses (classes will vary on a term-by-term basis,\u00a0 see list of classes ) Teach course in class, via zoom or on eCampus 1-5 days a week, depending on the course Schedule/Organize Lab courses as appropriate Schedule/Organize field trips, as appropriate Grade all assignments and homework for course Work with Head Advisor to collect required course documentation for accreditation. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: MA/MS or higher in Ecological, Environmental or Civil Engineering or related field. Evident commitment to inclusive excellence and educational equity. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of teaching excellence, such as student, peer or mentor evaluations. For distance education positions, experience with instruction of distance education courses. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Classroom and/or zoom instruction. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skill, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Human-Development-and-Family-Sciences_JR0000637-1": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Human Development and Family Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-17\nPart time\n\nDepartment: School of Human Development and Family Sciences Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed and considered as opportunities arise throughout the 2026/2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) Statement of Teaching - please upload as separate document. Finalists will be required to provide proof of their degree at the time of offer. The salary range listed reflects the full-time salary range and will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Linda Fenske linad.fenske@oregonstate.edu 541-737-4580 Job Summary: The School of Human Development and Family Sciences in the College of Health at Oregon State University invites applications for one or more fixed term, non-tenure track full/part-time Instructor positions to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Dean of Academic Affairs. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted \u00a0 when positions become available. In the College of Health we passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. We serve others, enjoy meaningful careers and lives, innovate, approach health and well-being through a lens of equity, and co-create knowledge and solutions to pressing health challenges in the far corners of Oregon, the nation and world. The primary mission of the Human Development and Family Sciences (HDFS) program is to discover and transmit knowledge that improves the health and well-being of individuals and families throughout their lifespan. HDFS has a large and very successful undergraduate program, which includes three degree options as well as multiple courses serving students from all OSU majors through the Baccalaureate Core. The School offers MS and PhD degrees, as well as an undergraduate major in HDFS available via E-campus. The curriculum encompasses human development and family studies classes. The program has nearly 1110 undergraduate majors (E-campus has approximately another 250) and 34 graduate majors. The faculty includes 25 members with areas of specialization that include family, adult development and aging, early childhood education, human development, human sciences, social policy, impact of poverty on families, gender and family relationships, and marriage and interpersonal relationships. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach and administer undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Critical Thinking in Human Development and Family Sciences, Applied Research Methods, or related areas. Hold regular office hours to assist students with coursework and answer questions regarding curriculum. May supervise graduate and undergraduate teaching assistants. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree or higher in Human Development & Family Studies, Psychology, Sociology, Early Childhood Education, Gerontology, or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks.* Teaching graduate level courses requires a PhD in Human Development, Family Studies, Early Childhood Education, Gerontology, or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Experience with modern pedagogical techniques. Ability to communicate effectively with a wide variety of audiences verbally and in writing. Evident commitment to educational equity. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Human Development, Family Studies, Early Childhood, Gerontology, or closely related discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Teaching experience at the college or university level. A demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence. Working Conditions/Schedule: Work schedule may vary depending upon student needs and engagement in campus and/or program activities. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor--PAC--Pool---2026-2027---SCUBA_JR0000514": {"title": "Instructor (PAC) Pool - 2026/2027:  SCUBA", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-14\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College o Health - Physical Activity Courses Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will continue to be consideration throughout the 2026/2027 academic year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) License/Certifications: Please attach as separate documents 4) Supplemental Questions: Please attach as a separate document a) Please list your total number of dives and the number of dives in a professional supervisory position. b) What is your philosophy in teaching beginners to dive? c) After reviewing the OSU mission statement at ( https://leadership.oregonstate.edu/trustees/about-board/oregon-state-university-mission-statement ) please state how your background and experience has prepared you to support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices. For additional information please contact: Katelyn Kirk katelyn.kirk@oregonstate.edu Starting salary within the salary range will be commensurate with education, experience, and training/certification. Starting salary range for the position of Instructor (PAC) is $32,100 \u2013 $39,233 pro-rated based on the number of classes taught per term. Finalists will be required to provide proof of their degree at the time of offer. Final candidates for this position must complete a sexual misconduct reference check, per University Policy 05-010. An offer of employment will be contingent upon satisfactory results from the sexual misconduct reference check. Job Summary: The SCUBA Activity Area in the Physical Activities Course (PAC) program, a part of the School of Exercise, Sport, and Health Sciences, in the College of Health at Oregon State University invites applications for one or more fixed term, non-tenure track full/part-time Instructor (PAC) positions to teach courses on a term-by-term basis for the 2026/2027 academic year. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacted when positions become available throughout the academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the program Director.\u00a0 We passionately believe that health is for all people. Our world-leading faculty and committed students work to prevent disease and injury, identify factors that affect health and well-being, inform policy, and shape environments that improve lives and help everyone, from children to seniors, thrive. We serve others, enjoy meaningful careers and lives, innovate, approach health and well-being through a lens of equity, and co-create knowledge and solutions to pressing health challenges in the far corners of Oregon, the nation and world. The primary mission of the\u00a0PAC\u00a0Program is to provide all Oregon State University students with the knowledge and experience to make sound decisions regarding present and future physically active lifestyles. The intent of the\u00a0PAC\u00a0Program is to provide quality instruction in safe, adequately equipped facilities and to create a positive, enjoyable learning environment. The\u00a0PAC\u00a0Instructor position will serve as an integral member of the\u00a0PAC\u00a0Program team, where each instructor plays a specific role to the larger organization. Recognizing individual interests and abilities, the program provides courses covering a wide variety of physical activities. We make an effort to address contemporary trends and student interests. Courses offered through the\u00a0PAC\u00a0Program may include but are not limited to classes in the Activity Areas of: Aquatics, Artistic & Social dance, Aerobics & Fitness Development, Martial arts, Mind/body, Outdoor Recreation, Resistance training, Sports, Yoga and Games. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES: Plan and organize instruction in ways that maximize student learning. Demonstrate a thorough and accurate knowledge of their field or discipline. Maintain familiarity with college and program goals, mission, and long-range plans Be accessible to colleges and students for advisement and consultation. Prepare, distribute, and submit syllabi and approved course outlines for all assigned sections in accordance with program and divisional policies. Participate in meetings and events required by the program administrators \u00a0 Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: All candidates must meet the following qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in any field. Current, valid Adult\u00a0CPR\u00a0and\u00a0AED Certification by the start of classes Current, valid First Aid certification by the start of classes Concussion training by the start of classes Evident commitment to educational equity. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Discipline Specific Demonstrated experience, knowledge and ability to instruct SCUBA courses Current and valid certification as a PADI Master SCUBA Diver Instructor 1+ years experience instructing SCUBA courses Current and valid driver\u2019s license. Current, valid Emergency O2 Certification by the start of classes Final candidates for this position must complete a sexual misconduct reference check, per University Policy 05-010. An offer of employment will be contingent upon satisfactory results from the sexual misconduct reference check. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. PREFERRED QAULIFICATIONS: Master's degree in any field Current and valid certification as a PADI Master SCUBA Diver Trainer, and/or Course Director 5+ years experience instructing SCUBA courses Current SCUBA cylinder inspector (PSI preferred) and experience and/or certification in SCUBA equipment formal annual service and general maintenance. Emergency O2 Certification CPR, FA, AED, and Emergency O2 Instructor Experience mentoring and certifying Dive Masters Successful teaching experience in a higher education setting, or equivalent Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Previous experience assessing student learning outcomes and curriculum development. Working Conditions/Schedule: In the performance of the duties of the position, incumbents will be required to lead physical activity courses and demonstrate activity-specific movements for a minimum duration of 50-110 minutes per scheduled class. Classes meet 1-3 times per week. \u2022 Ability to lift/carry SCUBA cylinders and full SCUBA rigs (50-80lbs.) and to demonstrate and teach dive rescue of adult victims \u2022 Ability to safely operate university Motor Pool vehicles, including \u00be ton pickup trucks and passenger vans \u2022 Requires working nights and/or weekends. Travel with students to open water sites and spending the night near dive sites is required. \u2022 This position requires working in water. Some work is required to be performed in an pool and/or outdoor environment, which may involve extreme temperature and weather conditions. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Anthropology_JR0000295": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Anthropology", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-14\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Liberal Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 Academic Year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and 2) Cover Letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position; and 3) Statement of Teaching For additional information, please contact: Lynn Roylance lynn.roylance@oregonstate.edu 541-737-3847 Job Summary: The Anthropology program in the School of Language, Culture, and Society invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track, full/part-time Instructor positions on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director.\u00a0 \u00a0 The Anthropology program at Oregon State University is committed to a four-field approach. The program offers an M.A., M.S., and PhD in Applied Anthropology. For more information, see http://oregonstate.edu/cla/anthropology. It is part of the School of Language, Culture, and Society, which also includes undergraduate and graduate programs in Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies; an undergraduate program and graduate minor in Ethnic Studies; minors in Indigenous Studies, Latinx Studies, Social Justice, Queer Studies; undergraduate majors and minors the World Languages & Cultures Program and a certificate in Food in Culture and Social Justice. Our School values interdisciplinary collaboration, community-centered research, and socially transformative learning. Key Responsibilities: Instruction Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in Anthropology or related field. \u00a0 Evident commitment to educational equity. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Anthropology or related field \u00a0 Demonstrated ability to design, \u00a0 teach \u00a0 and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote \u00a0 equitable \u00a0 teaching practices, to the \u00a0 benefit of all learners. \u00a0 Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Nuclear-Science-and-Engineering_JR0000247": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Nuclear Science and Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Engineering Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026\u20132027 Academic Year, as opportunities become available. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae \u00a0 2) A Cover Letter of Interest; indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position and how you meet each of the required qualifications and any preferred qualifications if applicable. 3) A Statement of Teaching 4) Publications 5) Transcripts Letters of Reference will be requested for those advanced to the reference stage. At that time, you will be asked to provide contact information for your referees who will be sent a secure quicklink that will allow them to upload the requested letters of reference on your behalf. For additional information please contact: Lizz Koch lizz.koch@oregonstate.edu 541-737-7063 \u00a0 Job Summary: The School of Nuclear Science and Engineering invites applications for part-time (varied \u00a0 FTE ), 9-month, fixed-term Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Head of School. The School of Nuclear Science & Engineering within the College of Engineering seeks temporary instructors to teach courses in the following areas: nuclear engineering, radiation health physics, radiochemistry or engineering science. May also include course/curriculum development. With a mission to provide world-class education that produces industry, academic, and policy leaders in the field of nuclear science, NSE boasts a robust graduate program with over 200 students. The curriculum covers various aspects of nuclear and radiation sciences, engineering, and technology. In addition, the School offers an acclaimed online Radiation Health Physics program, which ranks among the best in the nation. NSE's tenure/tenure-track faculty members specialize in a wide range of areas, such as nuclear reactor physics, thermal hydraulics, computational methods, radiation detection and measurement, nuclear security and nonproliferation, nuclear materials, health physics, and radiochemistry. Key Responsibilities: Instruct courses by using\u00a0appropriate\u00a0and various teaching strategies.\u00a0Acknowledge\u00a0differences in learning styles.\u00a0\u00a0 Communicates effectively, meets classes as scheduled, and\u00a0submits\u00a0grading\u00a0in a timely manner.\u00a0\u00a0 Complete ABET accreditation course assessment.\u00a0\u00a0 Participates\u00a0in departmental and college governance as well as any professional activities.\u00a0 Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Masters degree in nuclear engineering, radiation health physics, radiochemistry, or closely related field Good written and oral communication skills Preferred Qualifications: PhD in nuclear engineering, radiation health physics, radiochemistry, or closely related field Industrial research experience in nuclear engineering, radiation health physics, thermodynamics, thermal fluids, radiochemistry, or engineering science Teaching experience at the college or university level. A commitment to fostering environments that value different perspectives and experiences Working Conditions/Schedule: Office and classroom Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, knowledge, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Environmental-Sciences_JR0000624": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Environmental Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Office of Graduate Education Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 Academic Year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents:\u00a0 \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. 3) A Statement of Teaching- Upload as separate document. Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience.\u00a0 For additional information please contact: Mo Childers at Mo.Childers@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-2033. Job Summary: The Office of Graduate Education at OSU in Corvallis, Oregon, invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track part-time Instructors to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. \u00a0 Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Dean of Academic Affairs. Applications submitted to this recruitment pool are reviewed on an as needed basis. Qualified candidates will be contacte d\u00a0 when positions become available. \u00a0 Instructors may be needed to teach Corvallis campus and Ecampus courses in the following areas: graduate courses in Environmental Sciences (ENSC). The primary mission of the Environmental Sciences Graduate Program is to provide graduate education in Environmental Sciences. The curriculum encompasses most standard fields of the discipline. Key Responsibility: Administer and teach graduate courses in Environmental Sciences. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in discipline appropriate to the field of teaching/instructional tasks. Teaching or assistant experience at the college/university level. Evident commitment to educational equity. Preferred Qualifications: A PhD in a discipline appropriate to the field of teaching. Working Conditions/Schedule: Will be working in a classroom (physical or virtual) teaching Environmental Sciences graduate courses. Schedule will vary based upon course schedules and classroom availability. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Student-Success_JR0000575": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Student Success", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 Academic Year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and 2) Cover Letter describing; your experience, qualifications and interests that have prepared you to teach at the university level in the listed discipline(s); including which discipline(s) you are qualified to teach and the course modalities you are prepared to teach (online, in-person, and/or both). Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. For additional information, please contact: Sandra Neubaum sandy.neubaum@bus.oregonstate.edu (541) 713 8046 Job Summary: The College of Business invites applications for fixed-term, non-tenure track, full/part-time Instructors to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Dean . This position is responsible for the instruction, curriculum development, classroom management, and overseeing academic projects as part of the Student Success curriculum. This position will participate in strategic planning efforts that support the mission, vision, and goals for the College of Business as it pertains to the Student Success program. Key Responsibilities: Teach Student Success courses using inclusive, student-centered instructional practices that promote academic success and engagement. Develop course materials, curriculum, assessments, and classroom activities while supporting the delivery of Student Success programming. Plan and implement student success initiatives, including orientation, welcome week, and experiential learning opportunities that support student success. Provide individualized mentoring and holistic support to students while fostering an inclusive and welcoming learning environment. Participate in service activities that support the College, University, profession, and initiatives that advance diversity, equity, inclusion, and student success. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in Business, Education, College Student Services and Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited university. Experience with supporting students in their personal, professional and academic pursuits in a higher education setting. Demonstrated commitment to educational equity and a commitment to advancing the participation of diverse groups and supporting diverse perspectives. Demonstrated record of effective teaching at a high school level or accredited university. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, utilizing inclusive language and the ability to communicate with tact and diplomacy across diverse cultural boundaries. Excellent teamwork and collaboration skills. High computer proficiency; required qualifications include: strong MS office experience with Word, PowerPoint, Excel and working knowledge of Outlook and Windows/Mac. Ability to maintain professional decorum, as well as know or can demonstrate ability to learn and work within OSU system. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in utilizing best practices in retaining first year students in a higher education setting. An ability and willingness to learn new programs and applications quickly. Ability to juggle multiple tasks and responsibilities, prioritize appropriately, pay careful attention to details, and meet deadlines. Ability to work with ambiguity. Working Conditions/Schedule: The incumbent is responsible for maintaining a flexible work schedule. Some evenings and weekend work is required. Teaching assignments may include course delivery in any format \u2013 site-based in-person, asynchronous online, or hybrid combinations of online, site-based in-person, and/or remote instruction. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-12-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Spanish_JR0000523": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Spanish", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nPart time\n\nDepartment: World Languages and Cultures Program Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 Academic Year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: 1) A Curriculum Vitae; and 2) Cover Letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position; and 3) Statement of Teaching For additional information, please contact: Lynn Roylance lynn.roylance@oregonstate.edu 541-737-3847 Job Summary: The World Languages & Cultures Program invites applications for\u00a0one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track, full/part-time Spanish\u00a0Instructor\u00a0positions on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. The World Languages and Cultures program offers both in-person and online undergraduate majors and minors in Spanish, French, and German, as well as a\u00a0dual degree in Global Studies, minors in Linguistics and Japanese, and additional language instruction in ASL, Chinese, Italian, and Korean. It is part of the School of Language, Culture, and Society, which also includes undergraduate and graduate programs in Anthropology\u00a0& Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies; an undergraduate program and graduate minor in Ethnic Studies; minors in Indigenous Studies, Latinx Studies, Social Justice, Queer Studies;\u00a0and a certificate in Food in Culture and Social Justice. Our School\u00a0values interdisciplinary collaboration, community-centered research, and socially transformative learning.\u00a0\u00a0 Key Responsibilities: Instruction Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in \u00a0 Spanish \u00a0 or related field. \u00a0 Evident commitment to educational equity. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in \u00a0 Spanish \u00a0 or related field. Demonstrated ability to design, \u00a0 teach \u00a0 and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote \u00a0 equitable \u00a0 teaching practices, to the \u00a0 benefit of all learners. \u00a0 Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: $48,000 - $51,000 Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Women--Gender--and-Sexuality-Studies_JR0000522": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-07\n\nDepartment: Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 Academic Year. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position and how you meet each of the required qualifications and any preferred qualifications if applicable. 3) Statement of Teaching (upload as a separate document). \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Lynn Roylance at Lynn.Roylance@oregonstate.edu or 541-737-3847. Job Summary: The\u00a0 Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies program \u00a0in the School of Language, Culture, and Society invites applications for one or more fixed-term, non-tenure-track, full/part-time\u00a0Instructor\u00a0positions on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Director. Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies place women\u2019s concerns, gender analysis, and/or\u00a0LGBTQ\u00a0experience at the center of academic study. We recognize that gender and sexuality intersect with other categories of identity and experience, including race, ethnicity, social class, ability, and age. Our courses examine a wide range of topics from multidisciplinary perspectives. We encourage community involvement and activism, and our majors, minors, and graduate students complete internships with social change agencies and organizations. It is part of the School of Language, Culture, and Society, which also includes undergraduate and graduate programs in Anthropology; an undergraduate program and graduate minor in Ethnic Studies; minors in Indigenous Studies, Latinx Studies, Social Justice, Queer Studies; undergraduate majors and minors the World Languages & Cultures Program and a certificate in Food in Culture and Social Justice. Our School\u00a0values interdisciplinary collaboration, community-centered research, and socially transformative learning. Key Responsibilities: Instruction Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in WGSS or related field. Evident commitment to educational equity. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in WGSS or related field. Demonstrated ability to design, teach and assess courses that support inclusive learning principles and promote equitable teaching practices, to the benefit of all learners. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: $48,000 - $51,000 Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Management--Entrepreneurship---Strategy--and-Supply-Chain---Logistics-Management_JR0000460": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Management, Entrepreneurship & Strategy, and Supply Chain & Logistics Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-30\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026-2027 Academic Year as opportunities become available. When applying you will be required to attach: 1) A Curriculum Vita 2) A Cover Letter describing; your experience, qualifications and interests that have prepared you to teach at the university level in the listed discipline(s); including which discipline(s) you are qualified to teach and the course modalities you are prepared to teach (online, in-person, and/or both). For additional information please contact: Manuela Hoehn-Weiss Manuela.HW@oregonstate.edu (541) 737-3687 Job Summary: The College of Business invites applications for part-time (varied \u00a0 FTE ), 9-month, fixed-term Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Dean. Positions may teach in the area of Management, Entrepreneurship and Strategy, and/or Supply Chain and Logistics Management. The College of Business is committed to maintaining and enhancing its diverse and collaborative community that strives for equity and inclusivity. All faculty and staff members are responsible for helping to ensure that these goals are achieved and should be able to demonstrate contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Such contributions can be part of teaching, advising, service, and/or professional development. Outputs and impacts of these efforts to promote diversity, equity, and inclusion will be included in annual performance reviews and promotion dossiers. Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Management, Entrepreneurship and Strategy, and/or Supply Chain and Logistics Management using effective, inclusive, and student-centered instructional practices. Develop and deliver course content, assess student learning, provide feedback and support to students, and contribute to a positive learning environment that promotes student success. Engage in service activities that support the College, University, and professional community. Contribute to the College\u2019s commitment to inclusive excellence through teaching practices, student engagement, service, and professional development. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in appropriate business-related field. Demonstrated commitment to educational equity and a commitment to advancing the participation of diverse groups and supporting diverse perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in appropriate business-related field. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Evidence of educating and mentoring a diverse group of learners, which may include experience with serving on student thesis committees, directing internships, student mentoring or advising, service-learning courses, sponsoring clubs, or innovation pedagogies such as hybrid or online learning. Working Conditions/Schedule: Teaching assignments may include course delivery in any format \u2013 site-based in-person, asynchronous online, or hybrid combinations of online, site-based in-person, and/or remote instruction. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-12-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Accounting--Finance--and-Information-Systems_JR0000391": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Accounting, Finance, and Information Systems", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-30\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026\u20132027 Academic Year, as opportunities become available. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae \u00a0 2) A Cover Letter describing; your experience, qualifications and interests that have prepared you to teach at the university level in the listed discipline(s); including which discipline(s) you are qualified to teach and and the course modalities you are prepared to teach (online, in-person, and/or both). For additional information please contact: David Berger dave.berger@bus.oregonstate.edu (541) 737-2636 Job Summary: The College of Business invites applications \u00a0 for part-time (varied \u00a0 FTE ), 9-month, fixed-term Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Dean. Positions may teach in the area of Accounting, Finance or Business Information Systems. The College of Business is committed to maintaining and enhancing its diverse and collaborative community that strives for equity and inclusivity. All faculty and staff members are responsible for helping to ensure that these goals are achieved and should be able to demonstrate contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Such contributions can be part of teaching, advising, service, and/or professional development. Outputs and impacts of these efforts to promote diversity, equity, and inclusion will be included in annual performance reviews and promotion dossiers. Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Accounting, Finance or Business Information Systems using effective, inclusive, and student-centered instructional practices. Develop and deliver course content, assess student learning, provide feedback and support to students, and contribute to a positive learning environment that promotes student success. Engage in service activities that support the College, University, and professional community. Contribute to the College\u2019s commitment to inclusive excellence through teaching practices, student engagement, service, and professional development. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in appropriate business-related field. Demonstrated commitment to educational equity and a commitment to advancing the participation of diverse groups and supporting diverse perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in appropriate business-related field. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Evidence of educating and mentoring a diverse group of learners, which may include experience with serving on student thesis committees, directing internships, student mentoring or advising, service-learning courses, sponsoring clubs, or innovation pedagogies such as hybrid or online learning. Working Conditions/Schedule: Teaching assignments may include course delivery in any format \u2013 site-based in-person, asynchronous online, or hybrid combinations of online, site-based in-person, and/or remote instruction. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-12-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Marketing--Analytics-and-Design_JR0000390": {"title": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Marketing, Analytics and Design", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-30\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications will be considered throughout the 2026\u20132027 Academic Year, as opportunities become available. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Curriculum Vitae \u00a0 2) A Cover Letter of describing; your experience, qualifications and interests that have prepared you to teach at the university level in the listed discipline(s); including which discipline(s) you are qualified to teach and the course modalities you are prepared to teach (online, in-person, and/or both). For additional information please contact: Aimee Huff Aimee.Huff@oregonstate.edu (541) 737-3688 Job Summary: The College of Business invites applications for part-time (varied \u00a0 FTE ), 9-month, fixed-term Instructor positions to teach on a term-by-term basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Some of these appointments may be reviewed for renewal or transition to an instructional position on an annual basis at the discretion of the Dean. Positions may teach in the area of Marketing, Professional Sales, Business Analytics, Business Statistics, Business Law, Sports Business, Design & Innovation Management, Product & Merchandising Management, Interior Design and/or Apparel Design. The College of Business is committed to maintaining and enhancing its diverse and collaborative community that strives for equity and inclusivity. All faculty and staff members are responsible for helping to ensure that these goals are achieved and should be able to demonstrate contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Such contributions can be part of teaching, advising, service, and/or professional development. Outputs and impacts of these efforts to promote diversity, equity, and inclusion will be included in annual performance reviews and promotion dossiers. Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Marketing, Professional Sales, Business Analytics, Business Statistics, Business Law, Sports Business, Design & Innovation Management, Product & Merchandising Management, Interior Design and/or Apparel Design using effective, inclusive, and student-centered instructional practices. Develop and deliver course content, assess student learning, provide feedback and support to students, and contribute to a positive learning environment that promotes student success. Engage in service activities that support the College, University, and professional community. Contribute to the College\u2019s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion through teaching practices, student engagement, service, and professional development. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in appropriate business-related field. Demonstrated commitment to educational equity and a commitment to advancing the participation of diverse groups and supporting diverse perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in appropriate business-related field. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Evidence of educating and mentoring a diverse group of learners, which may include experience with serving on student thesis committees, directing internships, student mentoring or advising, service-learning courses, sponsoring clubs, or innovation pedagogies such as hybrid or online learning. Working Conditions/Schedule: Teaching assignments may include course delivery in any format \u2013 site-based in-person, asynchronous online, or hybrid combinations of online, site-based in-person, and/or remote instruction. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-12-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor_JR0000039": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-13\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by 10/1/26. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Resume/CV; including in bold the top five most relevant publications (please provide DOI when available). In-review or in-preparation (completed projects only) papers may be included as a citation in the CV list for early-career candidates if the projects and its findings are also referenced in your statement of research. The CV should clearly indicate experiences or accomplishments that support the minimum and preferred qualifications. \u00a0 2) A Cover letter; not to exceed 2 pages, that includes an executive summary of your research and teaching statements that addresses why your research and teaching is a strong fit for an integrative biology department that is seeking to bolster its expertise in organismal biology. 3) A Statement of Research; not to exceed 2 pages, that summarizes your research interests and vision. 4) A Statement of Teaching; not to exceed 1 page, that summarizes your teaching and mentorship experience, philosophy and inclusive, evidence-based practices. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Letters of Reference will be requested for those advanced to the reference stage. At that time, you will be asked to provide contact information for your referees who will be sent a secure quicklink that will allow them to upload the requested letters of reference on your behalf. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Tara Bevandich Tara.bevandich@oregonstate.edu 541-737-5336 Job Summary: The Department of Integrative Biology at Oregon State University (OSU) invites applications for three full-time (1.00 FTE), 9-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in the field of integrative biology. Oregon State University is a public R1 research university and the largest university in the state of Oregon, with an enrollment of over 35,000 students and a sponsored project research budget of over 400 million dollars in 2025. Within Oregon State, the College of Science is dedicated to research and education in exact and life sciences. The College is made of seven departments, deeply committed to upholding the values of inclusive excellence. Through our rich collection of people, ideas and perspectives, we engage in a healthy, constructive dialogue to learn, inform our research, and make discoveries. Successful candidates are expected to develop vigorous, externally funded research programs with a primary focus on understanding processes within organisms that drive performance. Organismal-level research that is integrated with and/or has clear implications for ecological or evolutionary processes is preferred. Research may include theoretical, experimental, comparative and/or observational approaches in laboratory and/or field settings. The candidates will also contribute to a vibrant, inclusive and collaborative department, including through mentorship of graduate and undergraduate students, teaching within the biology and zoology degree programs, and service to the university and profession. More information about the department is available at http://ib.oregonstate.edu . Key Responsibilities: Scholarship and Creative Activity Teaching, Advising and Other Assigned Duties Service Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Ph.D. (or foreign equivalent) in Biology or related field. Research with a primary focus on understanding processes within organisms that drive performance and may affect processes at ecological or evolutionary scales. Demonstrated ability or potential to establish an extramurally funded research program of high impact and longevity. Demonstrated ability or potential to instruct effectively using evidence-based practices at the undergraduate or graduate level Demonstrated ability or potential to mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated ability to collaborate with and engage with colleagues in a department, research or community group. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. Preferred (Special) Qualifications: Relevant post-doctoral experience, including academic or professional positions, and especially training that afford the candidate a unique, integrative perspective. Research that spans multiple biological levels or that utilizes multi-pronged approaches (e.g., field, laboratory, theory).\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Experience in interdisciplinary or transdisciplinary collaboration. Demonstrable commitment to inclusive teaching and mentorship practices. Experience teaching in multiple modalities, including traditional classroom, online and experiential settings. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: $85,000-$100,000 Anticipated Start Date: 2027-09-16 Anticipated End Date: We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Associate-Full-Professor--Psychological-Science_JR0001634": {"title": "Associate/Full Professor: Psychological Science", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nImportant Notifications: Application Deadline: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Current Employees: Do not apply via the OSU Career site. Instead, please login to your regular Workday account and visit the Jobs Hub to apply. Department: College of Liberal Arts - Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A Resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A Cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 3) A Statement of Research (upload as a separate document) 4) A Statement of Teaching (upload as a separate document) Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Jessee Dietch jessee.dietch@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The School of Psychological Science (housed within the College of Liberal Arts) at Oregon State University invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE) 9-month, tenure-track Associate or tenured Full Professor of Clinical Psychology position to assist in leading the emerging Clinical Science PhD program. Appointment at the Associate Professor rank is anticipated; however, appointment at a promoted rank may be considered depending upon the qualifications of the successful candidate. Any hiring at the rank of Associate Professor/Professor with indefinite tenure will be subject to a successful out-of-cycle tenure review process: https://academicaffairs.oregonstate.edu/resources-policies-legislation/policies-and-resources/promotion-and-tenure-guidelines/out-cycle . This position is part of a multi-line, multi-year investment in clinical science research and teaching, in support of a successful, rapidly growing undergraduate major and Ph.D. program. Clinical Science training was added in Fall 2024 as an option to our existing Psychology PhD program. Our Clinical Science model centers on rigorous training in the science and practice of evidence-based interventions, reaching diverse populations who may lack access to mental health care, and the wise use of technology in clinical psychological service. \u00a0 We seek a colleague who focuses on any area of clinical psychological science and is eager to join and help shape a dynamic team that prioritizes excellence in clinical research, practice, and training, consistent with Psychological Clinical Science Accreditation System (PCSAS) values. Key Responsibilities: Carry out an active program of research in an area of specialization Teach 4-5 classes each academic year, on a quarter system Mentor PhD students Perform service to the School, College, and University Perform service to the broader professional community Qualifications: Required Qualifications at the Rank of Associate OR Full Professor: Holds Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology, Clinical Science, or closely related field; Has an active, productive, and fundable research program in clinical psychological science, including a record of scholarship; Has a demonstrated record of working with a wide variety of students and/or faculty; Has a demonstrated commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence; Has a demonstrated commitment to open science practices; Has experience consistent with the values of Psychological Clinical Science Accreditation System (PCSAS) clinical science programs, including a commitment to inclusive excellence, and a record of producing PhD graduates who meet PCSAS standards of functioning as a clinical scientist (defined in this report: https://osf.io/preprints/psyarxiv/pyjwa_v1 ) Has a demonstrated record of excellence in graduate and/or undergraduate teaching; Meets the criteria for appointment at the associate level as detailed by the OSU Promotion & Tenure guidelines. See https://facultyaffairs.oregonstate.edu/faculty-handbook for details. OSU will consider previous years of experience at other, similar institutions towards timelines for rank promotions. Meets eligibility criteria for licensure as clinical psychologist in Oregon, including by a degree from an APA-, PCSAS- or CPA-accredited program and at least 1,500 supervised hours of post-degree work experience; Required Qualifications at the Rank of Full Professor: In addition, the candidate meets the criteria for appointment at the full professor level as detailed by the OSU Promotion & Tenure guidelines. See https://facultyaffairs.oregonstate.edu/faculty-handbook for details. OSU will consider previous years of experience at other, similar institutions towards timelines for rank promotions. Preferred Qualifications : Has experience serving in academic leadership roles; Has a record of successful, externally funded research that would help advance the goals of Prosperity Widely Shared: The Oregon State Plan, OSU Diversity Action Plan 2024-2030, and the College of Liberal Arts Strategic Plan; Has evidence of successful mentorship of early career faculty; Has demonstrated effectiveness in course development; Has demonstrated effectiveness in inclusive teaching Working Conditions/Schedule: Standard Monday to Friday work schedule, campus-based. Salary Range: Salary is commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2027-09-16 Anticipated End Date: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Union/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Natural-Resources_JR0001410": {"title": "Faculty Research Assistant: Natural Resources", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nImportant Notifications: Application Deadline: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Current Employees: Do not apply via the OSU Career site. Instead, please login to your regular Workday account and visit the Jobs Hub to apply. Department: College of Agricultural Sciences | Eastern Oregon Agricultural Research Center | Union Station - Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Sandy DeBano Sandy.debano@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The Eastern Oregon Agricultural Research Center - Union Station invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 12-month, fixed-term Faculty Research Assistant position. Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. We are seeking a Faculty Research Assistant to support ongoing research on forest and rangeland ecology and management. This position integrates forest monitoring data and environmental condition data to understand likely impacts of fuels thinning across the Meadow Creek watershed and Starkey Experimental Forest and Range as it relates to restoration and multiple use management objectives. This position will leverage broad scale monitoring efforts currently being implemented to directly inform management recommendations for watershed-level restoration. In addition, this position will provide centralized support for integration of forest and riparian monitoring data and current environmental condition data into various Research, Monitoring and Evaluation efforts across the Meadow Creek Restoration and Research Collaborative. Key Responsibilities: Scientific data collection Maintain research records Effectively communicate with research team Collaborate with external research partners Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in ecology, geography, natural resources, or related discipline. At least two years of experience working on natural resources-related issues in the Blue Mountains. Experience measuring and collecting natural resource and/or ecological data (e.g. soil, slope, aspect, richness, diversity, composition, density, etc.)\u00a0in field settings (forest, grassland, shrubland, wetlands, etc.). Experience using GPS units to navigate to locations and record spatial data in the field. Experience and commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. Strong written and oral communication and interpersonal skills. Working knowledge of MS Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Google Docs. Ability to kneel/squat for extended periods of time for data and sample collection. Ability and willingness to work in difficult terrain in adverse weather conditions (heat, snow, rain, etc.). Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in ecology, geography, natural resources, or related discipline. Knowledge of Starkey Experimental Forest and Range and the Pacific Northwest Research Station and the area around it. Familiarity with key partners in the region including USDA Forest Service, the Confederated Tribes of the Umatilla Indian Reservation, and Oregon Department of Fish and Wildlife. Experience working in multistakeholder projects with tribal, federal, state, and private stakeholders. Working knowledge of plant communities and plant species of the interior Pacific Northwest. Proficient in GIS and statistical applications (e.g. ArcGIS, R, Google Earth, Survey123, etc.). Experience writing reports and/or publications in addition to presenting and sharing findings to diverse audiences using a variety of formats. Working Conditions/Schedule: Employee in this position may be required lift, carry, push, and pull objects weighing up to 50 pounds. During field data collection, alternative work schedules may be required (e.g. 4 10-hour days). During the field season, camping in rural/remote locations (during the work week) may be required. Fieldwork occurs in the interior Pacific Northwest; terrain is mountainous and varies flat to steep and irregular (mountainous). Temperatures may fluctuate throughout the season from cold (below freezing) to very hot in the summer. Must work during inclement weather conditions. Salary Range: Salary to commensurate with education, training and experience Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Hermiston/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Assistant-Potato-Breeder_JR0001596": {"title": "Faculty Research Assistant: Assistant Potato Breeder", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nImportant Notifications: Application Deadline: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Current Employees: Do not apply via the OSU Career site. Instead, please login to your regular Workday account and visit the Jobs Hub to apply. Department: College of Agricultural Sciences | Hermiston Experiment Station - Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Femi Omilani, Ph.D. oluwafemi.omilani@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The Hermiston Agricultural Research & Extension Center (HAREC) invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 12-month, fixed-term Faculty Research Assistant position.\u00a0 Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. The Assistant Potato Breeder is responsible for supporting Oregon State University\u2019s Potato Breeding and Variety Development Program. This involves conducting greenhouse and field trials, performing crosses and evaluating experimental clones. The incumbent will also assist in the preparation of reports, grants and assist in extension events. This role will involve travel to other experimental stations and demands providing day-to-day direction to temporary employees and interaction with growers, industry partners and scientific audiences. The incumbent may prepare and present research materials and /or findings at professional meetings or in professional journals. \u00a0 This position requires driving a station vehicle to various field sites. Key Responsibilities: Field Experiments Greenhouse research Personal management for season and temporary employees Research data and publication Community service and outreach Qualifications: Required Qualifications: BS degree in Agronomy, Crop Science, Plant Science, Horticulture or a related field or BS degree in unrelated field and 7 years gathering, analysis and reporting of data in field crop research. Experience in operating farm or research-scale equipment. Experience working with Horticultural crops. Ability to lift, carry and pull objects up to 50 pounds and, occasionally, objects weighing more. Experience in commercial or research field crop management. Experience with computer spreadsheet and word processing programs. Demonstrated ability to work independently and with others. Evidence of strong written and verbal communication skills. Must possess or be able to obtain an Oregon Public Applicator\u2019s License and demonstration/research pesticide applicator\u2019s license within Three (3) months of employment and maintain throughout period of employment. Must possess or be able to obtain a farm endorsement within six (6) months of employment and maintain throughout the period of employment. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. \u00a0 This position requires driving a university vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the university; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a motor vehicle history check, possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions as per University Policy 05-030. Preferred Qualifications : Experience in potato or plant breeding. Experience in potato/vegetable production. Experience in molecular breeding and use of statistical and genetic tools. Experience towing trailers and hauling equipment. Experience in management of field crop production and research. Experience with field research techniques including plot design, maintenance and evaluation of field plots, seed processing, data collection and analysis and library research. Working Conditions/Schedule: This position involves field, greenhouse, laboratory and office work. Work schedules can vary dramatically depending on seasonal needs. Work outside of an 8-5 workday is not uncommon especially in the spring for planting and during harvest in the fall. Field and greenhouse work can be under temperature extremes. Field work may involve exposure to dusty, allergen-laden conditions. Hard physical activity involving lifting, pushing, and pulling objects weighing up to 50 lbs., and on some occasions, more than 50 lbs. Will operate university vehicles such as tractors, agricultural machinery, passenger vehicles and forklifts. Enter restricted areas such as confined spaces, biological laboratories and construction sites. Performs agricultural chemical applications (fungicide, herbicide, pesticide). Respirator or dust mask and other required protective equipment used as necessary. This position is deemed essential, and the incumbent will be expected to report to work during inclement weather, emergency and other University work curtailments or closures. Salary Range: Salary to commensurate with education, training and experience Anticipated Start Date: 2026-11-02 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor--Clinical-Skills_JR0001342": {"title": "Instructor: Clinical Skills", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nImportant Notifications: Application Deadline: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Current Employees: Do not apply via the OSU Career site. Instead, please login to your regular Workday account and visit the Jobs Hub to apply. Department: Veterinary Clinical Sciences - Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by October 30, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0 The salary range listed reflects the full-time salary range and will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Dr. Chris Cebra chris.cebra@oregonstate.edu 541-737-5568 Job Summary: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences within the Carlson College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a full-time (1.00 FTE), 9-month, fixed-term Instructor: Clinical Skills position.\u00a0 Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. \u00a0 The Carlson College of Veterinary Medicine provides professional and graduate programs for veterinary students leading to DVM, MS and PhD degrees, operates both a Large and a Small Animal Teaching Hospital (VTH), and a State Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory. The College operates within a total budget (from all sources) of approximately $36 million annually, which supports educational programs, veterinary medical and diagnostic public services, and research programs with broad impacts related to animal and human health. The Department of Clinical Sciences (DCS) oversees clinical, classroom, and laboratory teaching, and scholarly activity of clinical faculty and residents. \u00a0 The purpose of this position is to plan, conduct, assess and refine lectures and practical laboratories teaching clinical skills to veterinary students through experiential learning. The Department currently runs six distinct Clinical Skills courses each year over the three academic terms, and a variety of advanced courses. These provide training in a variety of clinical skills using lectures, live animals, animal tissues, inanimate models and various supplies and medical instruments, and are designed to meet curricular goals. The incumbent will be responsible for teaching in these courses, maintaining teaching laboratory facilities, supplies and equipment and ensuring compliance with appropriate safety and animal care protocols. This position contributes to the teaching mission of the Department, College and University by training future veterinarians. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES : Planning and conducting Clinical Skills Laboratories Qualifications: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: DVM or equivalent degree. 3 years of clinical experience in Small (dog, cat) or Large (ruminant, horse) Animal veterinary care, particular in primary care. Excellent oral and written communications skills Demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence. \u00a0 This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 24 months. \u00a0 \u00a0 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience with a broader range of species Teaching experience Experience in laboratory management, equipment supply procurement, record keeping and spreadsheet analysis. Working Conditions/Schedule: Labs are taught in a variety of environments. Small animal labs or those involving specimens or models are largely taught inside in a standard teaching laboratory. Large animal labs are in a larger range of environments, including outside or in barns or animal handling facilities. Some exercises occur in conventional seminar or lecture rooms. These labs involve exposure to live animals from a variety of species, tissue specimens, a variety of medical equipment, a range of chemical and biologic agents and the use of requisite safety equipment and protective equipment. Some afterhours work is required. Salary Range: Salary commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2026-12-16 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-15 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Union/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Eastern-Oregon-Agricultural-Research-Center--Union-Experiment-Station_JR0001521": {"title": "Faculty Research Assistant: Eastern Oregon Agricultural Research Center, Union Experiment Station", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nImportant Notifications: Application Deadline: When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. Current Employees: Do not apply via the OSU Career site. Instead, please login to your regular Workday account and visit the Jobs Hub to apply. Department: Eastern Oregon Agricultural Research Center, Union Experiment Station - Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: \u00a0 1) A resume/CV; and \u00a0 2) A cover letter indicating how your qualifications and experience have prepared you for this position. \u00a0\u00a0 Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. \u00a0 For additional information please contact: Bryan Endress Bryan.endress@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The Eastern Oregon Agricultural Research Center, Union Experiment Station invites applications for two full-time (1.00 FTE), 12-month, fixed-term Faculty Research Assistant positions.\u00a0Reappointment is at the discretion of the Department Head. These positions are located in Union, Oregon. We are seeking two botanist/plant ecologists to support ongoing research on forest and rangeland ecology and management. These positions will support multiple projects including: 1) research with Oregon Department of Fish and Wildlife focused on mule deer forage availability and habitat quality, and 2) the ecology, management and restoration of First Foods, particularly Roots and Berries in partnership with Confederated Tribes of the Umatilla Indian Reservation, Nez Perce Tribe, land management agencies (e.g. Forest Service) and non-governmental organizations and 3) evaluating and assessing responses of riparian, grassland and forest ecosystems to various restoration and management treatments in partnership with the Pacific Norwest Research Station and others. These positions play key roles in projects, including collecting a range of environmental, natural resource, and ecological attributes in the field, implementing field and lab experiments (e.g. seed germination studies), collaborating with ecologists, land managers and stewards, as well as assisting with data analysis and contributing to and authoring publications, reports, presentations and outreach materials. These positions work closely with project partners in all aspects of the work. \u00a0 The Eastern Oregon Agricultural Research Center (EOARC) is composed of two separate and fully functional research stations \u2013 Burns and Union Stations. The Union Station is Oregon State University\u2019s first branch research station (established in 1901). Research and outreach activities are focused on rangeland ecology and management, wildlife management, ecological restoration, alternative livestock systems and sustainable resource management in the diverse landscapes of eastern Oregon.\u00a0EOARC faculty and staff collaborate on research and outreach efforts with a wide range of partners including agencies, tribes and non-governmental organizations.\u00a0\u00a0 Key Responsibilities: Scientific data collection Maintain research records Effectively communicate with research team Collaborate with external research partners Measure a variety of ecological and natural resource variables Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in ecology, botany, plant ecology, natural resources, rangeland ecology, wildlife or related discipline. Experience measuring and collecting natural resource and/or ecological data (e.g. soil, slope, aspect, richness, diversity, composition, density, etc.)\u00a0in field settings (forest, grassland, shrubland, wetlands, etc.). Experience using GPS units to navigate to locations and record spatial data in the field. Experience and/or training in use of dichotomous keys, plant identification and plant/vegetation measurements. Experience and commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. Strong written and oral communication and interpersonal skills. Working knowledge of MS Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Google Docs. Ability to lift, carry, push, and pull objects weighing up to 50 pounds. Ability to kneel/squat for extended periods of time for data and sample collection. Ability and willingness to work in difficult terrain in adverse weather conditions (heat, snow, rain, etc.). This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months. This position requires driving a university vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the university; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a motor vehicle history check, possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions as per University Policy 05-030. Preferred Qualifications : A demonstrable commitment to inclusive excellence. Master\u2019s Degree in ecology, botany, plant ecology, natural resources, rangeland ecology, wildlife or related discipline. Experience or knowledge of seed germination and plant propagation techniques. Working knowledge of plant communities and plant species of the interior Pacific Northwest. Proficient in GPS, GIS and statistical applications (e.g. ArcGIS, R, Google Earth, Survey123, Avenza, etc.). Experience collecting data in the field using tablets, smart phones and/or rugged computers. Experience in and knowledge of Traditional Ecological Knowledge / Indigenous Knowledge, decolonizing methodologies and approaches, ethics related to knowledge co-production and collaborating with indigenous partners. Experience driving 4WD vehicles on dirt/gravel roads. Experience in data management and analysis. Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience. Anticipated Start Date: 2027-01-04 Anticipated End Date: 2027-06-30 When applying, please keep in mind this posting will close at 11:59 pm the night before the posted \"end date\". Applications MUST be submitted prior to this deadline. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has \u201ccritical or security-sensitive\u201d responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU\u2019s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."}}, "rows": {"https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Horticulture_JR0001467": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Horticulture_JR0001467", "job_title_in_post": "Faculty Research Assistant: Horticulture", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Agricultural Sciences perform field research", "area_key_words": "Horticulture", "deadline_of_application": "October 31, 2026", "posted_date": "2026-10-16", "position_start_date": "2027-01-11"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Botany---Plant-Pathology--Internal-Employment-Opportunity-_JR0001485": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Botany---Plant-Pathology--Internal-Employment-Opportunity-_JR0001485", "job_title_in_post": "Faculty Research Assistant: Botany & Plant Pathology (Internal Employment Opportunity)", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Botany & Plant Pathology (Internal Employment Opportunity", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-16"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Newport-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Marine-Mammal-Institute-GEMM-Lab_JR0001383": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Newport-Campus/Faculty-Research-Assistant--Marine-Mammal-Institute-GEMM-Lab_JR0001383", "job_title_in_post": "Faculty Research Assistant: Marine Mammal Institute-GEMM Lab", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Marine Mammal Institute-GEMM Lab", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-16", "position_start_date": "2026-11-02"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027---Nutrition_JR0001588": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027---Nutrition_JR0001588", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool - 2026-2027:  Nutrition", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Nutrition and Public Health", "area_key_words": "Nutrition", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-15", "position_start_date": "2026-10-13"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Environmental---Occupational-Health-and-Safety_JR0001587": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Environmental---Occupational-Health-and-Safety_JR0001587", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool - 2026-2027: Environmental & Occupational Health and Safety", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Nutrition and Public Health", "area_key_words": "Environmental & Occupational Health and Safety", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-15", "position_start_date": "2026-10-13"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Social-Work_JR0001554": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Social-Work_JR0001554", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Social Work", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "College of Education in the Social Work Major", "area_key_words": "Social Work; Education course", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-15", "position_start_date": "2026-10-12"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Health-Management---Policy_JR0001569-1": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Health-Management---Policy_JR0001569-1", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Health Management & Policy", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Nutrition and Public Health", "area_key_words": "Health Management & Policy", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-13", "position_start_date": "2026-10-12"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool----2026-2027--Health-Promotion---Behavior_JR0001555": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool----2026-2027--Health-Promotion---Behavior_JR0001555", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool -  2026/2027: Health Promotion & Behavior", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Nutrition and Public Health", "area_key_words": "Health Promotion & Behavior", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-13", "position_start_date": "2026-10-09"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Global-Health_JR0001553": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Global-Health_JR0001553", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Global Health", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Nutrition and Public Health", "area_key_words": "Global Health", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-13", "position_start_date": "2026-10-09"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor_JR0001433": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor_JR0001433", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Biochemistry and Biophysics in the College of Science", "area_key_words": "highly interdisciplinary environment; molecular biology; creating innovative coursework aligned", "deadline_of_application": "November 30, 2026", "posted_date": "2026-10-13", "position_start_date": "2027-09-07"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Counselor-Education_JR0001509-1": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Counselor-Education_JR0001509-1", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool - 2026/2027: Counselor Education", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "College of Education in the Counseling Major", "area_key_words": "Counselor Education", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-12", "position_start_date": "2026-10-07"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Epidemiology_JR0001526": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--Epidemiology_JR0001526", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool - 2026-2027: Epidemiology", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Nutrition and Public Health", "area_key_words": "Epidemiology", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-12", "position_start_date": "2026-10-08"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor--Extension-Plant-Pathology_JR0001109": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor--Extension-Plant-Pathology_JR0001109", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor: Extension Plant Pathology", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Botany and Plant Pathology within the College of Agricultural Sciences", "area_key_words": "Extension Plant Pathology", "deadline_of_application": "November 6, 2026", "posted_date": "2026-10-12", "position_start_date": "2026-11-30"}, "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--English--Writing--Film--and-Applied-Journalism_JR0001312": {"school_id": 1107, "posting_url": "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Instructor-Pool---2026-2027--English--Writing--Film--and-Applied-Journalism_JR0001312", "job_title_in_post": "Instructor Pool \u2013 2026/2027: English, Writing, Film, and Applied Journalism", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "English, Writing, Film, and Applied Journ